{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream","id":1501283,"title":"Do you think VTM will ever become mainstream?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-24T17:15:41-08:00","id":1501283,"title":"Do you think VTM will ever become mainstream?","content":"I have a hard time believing that something like that will ever happen as most people would rather play video games and may not be willing to sit down and play a TTRPG, even if it is through an online platform. Many people these days don't even know what a TTRPG is.<br /> <br /> What about you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T17:48:32-08:00","id":1501288,"title":"","content":"A better question to ask is what does a TTRPG bring to the table that a Video Game doesn't?<br /> <br /> A video game, when competently made, offers a far superior experience when it comes to combat. The computer handles all the mechanics and rules interactions, you just click away to your heart's content. Now the question of FPS, Third Person Shooter, MOBA style, etc. is a personal taste thing, but overall, anything that takes the mechanics heavy lifting off the Players is a good thing.<br /> <br /> What a TTRPG or Online TTRPG does better than a video game is narrative options. If you want to play out a story where it is horror, depression, and nothing but picking the lesser of a dozen evils, you can. But you can take the same rules and mechanics and run a game that is practically a vampire superheroes game, or run an anime inspired slapstick game.<br /> <br /> But here is the problem, most people are tired, they are stressed out, they have limited time to themselves for gaming. When you are in that sort of state, you are looking for a round or two of Vampire Survivors which can be played with one thumb stick. They won't have the energy or interest in playing out a sprawling epic of empire building, sagas of love and betrayal, or whatever else players can't get out of playing a few rounds of Dota or Smite.<br /> <br /> Be it VtM or D&amp;D, the main issue is that to be truly mainstream, mechanics need to support both the brain dead just want to chill for an hour before going to sleep crowd and support those rarer individuals who can allocate the mental energy and time to run games for 6+ hours multiple times a week. If anything, this is why RP streams like Critical Role is popular, it allows a viewer to participate in a game without putting energy into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T19:55:56-08:00","id":1501295,"title":"","content":"What are your metrics for mainstream? TTRPGs are more mainstream now than they've ever been. Even if most people have never played one, they can recognize D&amp;D being played if it's happening in a film or TV show. Major IPs that have no need to branch out into the TTRPG realm to maintain their brands are getting TTRPG books right now.<br /> <br /> Video game are more popular for a lot of reasons: one of which is that everything from Candy Crush to Dark Souls falls into that umbrella. Casual 'brain dead' games can be on your Steam account next to incredibly mentally intense ones. The more popular RPGs are more intense ones, and thus casual ones aren't really thought about by most people if they need something easy and lowkey; but those TTRPGs do exist.<br /> <br /> Though I don't agree with Thoth's pessimism. People want social experiences with other people. The pandemic has made that more true, not less. Shifting values among younger generations are also shifting in the same direction: experiences over &quot;stuff.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T23:15:52-08:00","id":1501302,"title":"","content":"Lol no. Not in its current state anyway, they can't even generate mass appeal in their own fandom for 5th ed. 6th would have to be an absolute banger to even move towards that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T00:39:30-08:00","id":1501305,"title":"","content":"It would also help if VtM could get another major video game, to revive brand recognition. Much like how a whole generation of people knew about VtM through the original Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> If the sequel ever actually materializes, it might do it. <i>IF</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T04:34:44-08:00","id":1501310,"title":"","content":"Humans have been telling eachother stories for thousands of years. These &quot;Vidya games&quot; are just a fad, like personal cars. (off topic: moving away from cars seems to be a small and positive trend) <br /> <br /> <br /> VTM really is an amazing thing for a generation of doomers, but unfortunately the last edition has really succeeded in making a divisive product and sacrificed it's mass appeal. IF the WoD gets it's act together, I see no reason why it won't be a huge thing 20 years from now, but until then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T04:37:10-08:00","id":1501311,"title":"","content":"The appetite is certainly out there. Bloodhunt hit 29K people on its best day. It might not have lasted, but the brand brought a pretty big number of people into a new game in an insanely crowded part of the video game market. As I linked to in a different thread Swansong got panned last year; but lets be honest the &quot;worst video games of 2022&quot; really means, &quot;the worst video games or games from brands that people have actually heard about.&quot; If there wasn't some desire for VtM out there, people wouldn't have noticed Swansong enough to care if it was good or bad.<br /> <br /> While I think everyone here knows what I think of the odds of this happening are, this is currently actually a really good window for the WoD and VtM to get back in there. The OGL debacle has gotten a lot of attention to the idea that there are games besides D&amp;D out there. VtM still has a lot of nostalgia value to it. Bloodlines 1 remains a regular game in the &quot;cult classics everyone should try,&quot; lists out there. The right product before the window closes could do wonders for making VtM something talked about among bigger audiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T05:43:41-08:00","id":1501312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501311#post1501311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I think everyone here knows what I think of the odds of this happening are, this is currently actually a really good window for the WoD and VtM to get back in there. The OGL debacle has gotten a lot of attention to the idea that there are games besides D&amp;D out there. VtM still has a lot of nostalgia value to it. Bloodlines 1 remains a regular game in the &quot;cult classics everyone should try,&quot; lists out there. The right product before the window closes could do wonders for making VtM something talked about among bigger audiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this OGL debacle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T11:15:52-08:00","id":1501329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream#post1501283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time believing that something like that will ever happen as most people would rather play video games and may not be willing to sit down and play a TTRPG, even if it is through an online platform. Many people these days don't even know what a TTRPG is.<br /> <br /> What about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there will always be room for both myself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-25-2023, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T12:30:44-08:00","id":1501335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501295#post1501295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I don't agree with Thoth's pessimism. People want social experiences with other people. The pandemic has made that more true, not less. Shifting values among younger generations are also shifting in the same direction: experiences over &quot;stuff.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What part of my post was pessimistic?<br /> <br /> Hard times and social isolation make people want to strengthen social connections, but at the same time the worse the times are, the less time you have for indulgences, so after working two jobs, fixing food for the family, doing chores, catching up on bills, etc. the only thing you will have energy to do is sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T13:10:17-08:00","id":1501338,"title":"","content":"I'm really confused to what you mean by &quot;mainstream&quot; here? Like TTRPGs are pretty mainstream like you have massive shows like Critical Role and even VtM has one in L.A. By Night. VtM got a TV show made, it only lasted a season but hey it still was on TV. D&amp;D is getting that movie and in the past other movies have used 'offbrand' TTRPGs to how Nerds having fun.<br /> <br /> Is VtM ever going to be at a point to over take D&amp;D? I think we are at an interesting point where D&amp;D is on its last legs. With WotC pushing D&amp;D to be a billion dollar property and thus monetizing every part of it to try to squeeze out every buck they can, I think other TTRPG IPs have a chance to gain a lot more time in the spot light.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T16:34:06-08:00","id":1501353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501312#post1501312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is this OGL debacle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hasbro/WotC is making a new OGL for D&amp;D Beyond, but they want to have it invalidate the old OGL. An early draft of the new one got linked and was full of horrible stuff that Hasbro/WotC have walked back, but they're still trying to make all old OGL material &quot;invalid&quot; as OGL. This lead to huge backlash among the vast third party industry around D&amp;D, from people that make custom monster blocks, to big players like Critical Role. There has been a sizeable number of cancellations of D&amp;D Beyond accounts in response (to the point where WotC changed the website to make it harder to cancel your subscription to stem the tide), and despite attempts to mollify the community with press releases about the new OGL, all of the voices with platforms that made this something that got to bigger audiences for D&amp;D are still telling people WotC is not doing right by the community and fans.<br /> <br /> Paizo has already jumped in with &quot;ORC&quot; their own open license, with a lot of support from other prominent OGL-based RPG companies, and even ones that don't use d20 for their flagship games, and is poised to reclaim their status as actual competition for WotC based on how poorly this has been going on the PR front.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501335#post1501335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What part of my post was pessimistic?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's general very of macro-economics, how poverty doesn't actually stop people from seeking entertainment because it's a vital part of emotional heath, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T17:03:28-08:00","id":1501356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501338#post1501338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really confused to what you mean by &quot;mainstream&quot; here? Like TTRPGs are pretty mainstream like you have massive shows like Critical Role and even VtM has one in L.A. By Night. VtM got a TV show made, it only lasted a season but hey it still was on TV. D&amp;D is getting that movie and in the past other movies have used 'offbrand' TTRPGs to how Nerds having fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say mainstream, I mean something most people will know and understand. Many people I have talked to dont seem to have actually heard of VTM, but a few have heard of DND. However, it seems that many who have heard of DND dont seem to actually play it. I have only met a few who actually have played the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501338#post1501338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is VtM ever going to be at a point to over take D&amp;D? I think we are at an interesting point where D&amp;D is on its last legs. With WotC pushing D&amp;D to be a billion dollar property and thus monetizing every part of it to try to squeeze out every buck they can, I think other TTRPG IPs have a chance to gain a lot more time in the spot light.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Very few people, the ones I have spoken with anyway, seem to even know what a TTRPG is, coupled with the fact that not everyone will be able to align their schedules to play a session. Its kind of similar to when you are trying to get a study group together, people will have difficulty finding a date that suits everybody.<br /> <br /> Perhaps other TTRPGs could gain a lot more spotlight, but I dont really know how probable it is, especially these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 01-25-2023, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T17:43:04-08:00","id":1501362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501305#post1501305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would also help if VtM could get another major video game, to revive brand recognition. Much like how a whole generation of people knew about VtM through the original Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> If the sequel ever actually materializes, it might do it. <i>IF</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully bloodlines 2 is actually good, but its already 2023 and im pretty sure a lot of the hype is gone by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-15-2023, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T18:16:20-08:00","id":1501365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501356#post1501356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say mainstream, I mean something most people will know and understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of Americans are only vaguely aware of the sport cricket, and probably don't understand the rules of it at all. But it's also the second most popular sport to watch on Earth.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of bias in what counts as &quot;mainstream&quot; if you're just going to try for some sort of &quot;most people&quot; standard, because you're not sampling most people. To most people on Earth, American football in a niche sport on a few people care about, while soccer is the sport &quot;everyone&quot; knows. In the US, football is hugely mainstream, and soccer is a niche sport that continues to struggle to try to get a serious following in the country.<br /> <br /> The number of things that are mainstream is minuscule when you need 4 billion people to know and understand something for it to be mainstream.<br /> <br /> You might need to reconsider how to to define mainstream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T19:01:36-08:00","id":1501368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501365#post1501365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vast majority of Americans are only vaguely aware of the sport cricket, and probably don't understand the rules of it at all. But it's also the second most popular sport to watch on Earth.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of bias in what counts as &quot;mainstream&quot; if you're just going to try for some sort of &quot;most people&quot; standard, because you're not sampling most people. To most people on Earth, American football in a niche sport on a few people care about, while soccer is the sport &quot;everyone&quot; knows. In the US, football is hugely mainstream, and soccer is a niche sport that continues to struggle to try to get a serious following in the country.<br /> <br /> The number of things that are mainstream is minuscule when you need 4 billion people to know and understand something for it to be mainstream.<br /> <br /> You might need to reconsider how to to define mainstream.</div> </div> </div> </div>And when the country with around 330 million people has an entertainment industry which influences the other 7.6+ billion people on the planet, mainstream is what the masses are told it is.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong though, I agree with the sentiment that reality is a collection of smaller bubbles rather than one large bubble that is shared, but throwing around numbers as proof of what mainstream can miss other realities that are equally if not more important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T01:11:14-08:00","id":1501381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501368#post1501368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And when the country with around 330 million people has an entertainment industry which influences the other 7.6+ billion people on the planet, mainstream is what the masses are told it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The US isn't the only country with influence on global cultural trends. US media companies regularly self-edit material in order to satisfy both official and unofficial standards to get widespread releases in countries like China. Anime and K-pop are both examples of the US exporting a cultural element to other people, only for them to redo it into a unique new thing, and then export that back to the US in a fashion that then influences our media industries.<br /> <br /> The number of overlapping bubbles trying to push media expressions into the mainstream is far too convoluted to simplify to the idea that the US is just telling everyone else what &quot;mainstream&quot; is. As the examples you responded to illustrate, the US's influence is not such that it just gets to tell people what mainstream is, because the masses have not just rolled over an accepted that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't get me wrong though, I agree with the sentiment that reality is a collection of smaller bubbles rather than one large bubble that is shared, but throwing around numbers as proof of what mainstream can miss other realities that are equally if not more important. </div> </div> </div>When did I advocate &quot;throwing numbers around,&quot; to prove what is and isn't mainstream? The only objective numbers I put up is a simple truth: if most people on Earth is your metric, that means over 4 billion people need to meet the criteria in question, because that's the minimum for being most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T01:44:15-08:00","id":1501384,"title":"","content":"IDK if there's one thing that years of experiencing American culture via hollywood and the news I have learned it's that American culture is <i>weird*, </i>even as someone who's moved around and seen a lot and who's job is to talk to everyone from everywhere. Why do their schools have lockers everywhere? Why is the drinking age so high that everyone's expected not to follow it? It's kind of horrifying that their infrastructure is so bad that getting a car at 16 is cool and normal.... and so on and so forth. (ok that last one applies to a few other places but anyhow) There's a lot of low hanging fruit and it's really impossible to see the country as &quot;normal&quot;, even if constant exposure and English use makes it a more familiar weird rather than an exotic weird. <br /> <br /> <i>obviously, the USA is a big and disconnected place, and some parts are weirder than others. </i><br /> <br /> That said, the many dysfunctions of the USA make it one of the most perfect settings for VTM and WTA, and I guess to an extent these are features that make US movies more interesting: <i>Breaking Bad</i> is very much a product of the US and it would be hard to see the conditions that made Walter White in Europe. VTM becomes significantly less interesting when taking place in a society that has things sorted: There's not really much you can get away with in Utrecht or Vienna or Santiago, and I hold to the idea that in the WoD the nordics are so nice because short summer nights keep the vampires out. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the WoD speaks greatly to the zeitgeist that everything's getting worse, and that even if things are &quot;getting better&quot;, we're really just on the way to losing our jobs to automation and living in debt slavery as our rents will rise to the point where we can't pay them even if we exceed nine people per room. Vampires are parasites, Landlords are parasites: we're dealing in universal truths here. VTM not being something everyone's heard of is some extreme mismanagement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T09:08:42-08:00","id":1501406,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem I see to the WoD getting back into a sort of mainstream limelight is that while it captured the Zeitgeist of the 90\u2019s and rode it like a champ, it hasn\u2019t done nearly so well adapting to the Zeitgeist as it has continued to evolve.<br /> <br /> A biggie in this regard is it\u2019s failure to acknowledge that the rebels of the 90\u2019s are now the establishment of today. The edginess of 90\u2019s LGBT culture is now normal and celebrated by mainstream culture in the 2020\u2019s. Media that doesn\u2019t offer inclusion is lambasted in pop culture and the \u201cMoral Majority\u201d of the 80s/90s is a punchline in the modern days of clerical abuse scandals.<br /> <br /> The 90\u2019s rebels are the now the CEO\u2019s and politicians able to enact their beliefs through things like Diversity Equity and Inclusion and Environmental Social Governance scores to shape how businesses and organizations operate.<br /> <br /> Trying to claim the same social outcasts of the 90\u2019s are still the oppressed outcasts just doesn\u2019t ring true and without truth you\u2019re never going to be able to capture that ephemeral thing that is the Zeitgeist that will ride you into the mainstream.<br /> <br /> If you ask me, the present spirit of the age is Atomization. Social media connects the world more tightly, but our youth have never felt more disconnected from each other within its web. The ability to define your own meaning for everything has led to a devaluation of even the concept of \u201cmeaning.\u201d Teens are committing suicide at epidemic rates because they can\u2019t find meaning in their own lives or fail to live up the impossible ideals of social media influencers and have few friends outside of their social media accounts.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the world grows darker and their futures more uncertain; environmental and economic collapse, pandemics and escalating wars. They fear forming families and having children of their own because of what they believe they\u2019d be bringing that child into. A youth of today could be forgiven for believing the Apocalypse is at their doorstep.<br /> <br /> Isolation and fear are the Zeitgeist of the present age, IMHO. If VtM wants to be mainstream again in the present day, it needs to offer material that speaks to that spirit; either in offering hope/purpose (ex. play up Clan as family and a way to be part of something\u2026 perhaps more mono-Clan scenarios in books) or in reaffirming their fears as valid (ex. not great for a ttrpg, but in a video game the idea of isolation and impending doom is something easy to work with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T10:55:23-08:00","id":1501415,"title":"","content":"Just a curious question from the compartive newbie. How well know is Vampire The Masquerade outside the gaming circles? Most people know what D&amp;D and Magic The Gathering is due to some rather biased media coverage back in the day trying to push a satanic narrative that got debunked by law enforcement later. Is our game on the same level in terms of name recognition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T10:59:40-08:00","id":1501416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501415#post1501415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a curious question from the compartive newbie. How well know is Vampire The Masquerade outside the gaming circles? Most people know what D&amp;D and Magic The Gathering is due to some rather biased media coverage back in the day trying to push a satanic narrative that got debunked by law enforcement later. Is our game on the same level in terms of name recognition?</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD used to be fairly well known outside gaming circles. In terms of biased media coverage, Steven Colbert had a guest on The Colbert Report that did VtM LARP and dressed up Dracula and they talked about it a bit. But I don't think that recognition stayed around as well as D&amp;D did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T12:00:59-08:00","id":1501419,"title":"","content":"Vampire is still on the fringes of pop-culture relevance. It's nowhere near where it used to be, but given it was the second biggest brand in RPGs and had a lot of crossover into general pop culture in the 90s/early 00s, a lot of Gen X and Millenials probably have it somewhere in their head; and are starting to replace Boomers as the heads of companies/etc.<br /> <br /> Like, if you Googling &quot;the Vampire Murders,&quot; you're probably getting the Rod Ferrell case as one of your first hits. He might not be getting a Netflix true crime miniseries any time soon, but I usually see references to the case in wider geek cultural spaces in some sort of &quot;geek true crime trivia&quot; sort of context at least once or twice a year. So that impact from the VtM golden age hasn't completely faded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T14:35:07-08:00","id":1501427,"title":"","content":"In germany as far as I recocnized it is still relative well known. While it is not as famous as D&amp;D, DSA (the german D&amp;D clone that became a thing of itself), Shadowrun and Pathfinder, it is at least something people can get on with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T15:44:38-08:00","id":1501434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501381#post1501381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did I advocate &quot;throwing numbers around,&quot; to prove what is and isn't mainstream? The only objective numbers I put up is a simple truth: if most people on Earth is your metric, that means over 4 billion people need to meet the criteria in question, because that's the minimum for being most people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the 4 billion people you mentioned are not as important in the global mainstream sense as the few hundred thousand people who work as the main decision makers of Hollywood, Gaming, Music, etc.<br /> <br /> Mainstream is one part numbers, one part monetization, one part level of being vocal about things. Yellowstone was one of, if not the most watched TV show recently, yet most social media didn't even have it on the radar for being relevant enough to bring up. Why? Because the demographic for the people watching the show were not on social media.<br /> <br /> If you create a product that 4 billion people like, but only a few hundred thousand people will buy, then it doesn't matter how mainstream you are because of the requirement of commercial success. In such a scenario, everyone will agree the concept is cool and rip it off until someone comes up with a variant that is more relevant in the current market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T16:17:11-08:00","id":1501438,"title":"","content":"You seem to be skipping that was I advising to <b>not</b> use &quot;most people on Earth&quot; as a metric for mainstream because 4 billion people being into something clearly isn't how things work. So I'm not sure what point you're trying to make on that.<br /> <br /> Your insistence on the primacy of the US/English language media footprint seems to completely ignore how much India, China, South Korea, and other countries are starting to really push themselves into global entertainment instead of just focusing on internal national audiences. Hollywood did not decide to make Demon Slayer: Mugen Train the highest grossing film of 2020.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T03:28:44-08:00","id":1501454,"title":"","content":"When it comes to business, concentration is sometimes more valuable than spread. The superbowl makes more money than the World Cup despite being a smaller event. It's way easier to go for a specific demographic rather than everyone everywhere all at once, and it's easier for companies to advertise towards people they can actually cater to. As much as I loved the few pieces of choice Indian cinema I've watched they're far too much a product of where they're from and they make artistic decisions which could be baffling, if not alienating to outsiders. Similar things could be said for Japanese and Korean products, while the middle kingdom has the whole dicatorship thing going on. Also, As interesting it is to see my father in law eternally watching Korean historical dramas dubbed in Russian, I don't imagine he has the same sense of attraction a Korean would to certain stars or directors. <br /> <br /> Besides, I don't really think the WoD should be thinking about tackling India when they can't even handle their home turf. I'm aware some things become more popular outside of their home, but that's almost always by happy accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T11:07:24-08:00","id":1501469,"title":"","content":"I've been watching lots of South Korean, Hong Kong action and Wuxia flicks and like MyWifeIsScary noted its a niche genre and won't get much exposure in mainstream entertainment. I remember when Critical Drinker gave his review on RRR and you have to pretty open minded to really enjoy storytelling from another culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T15:56:51-08:00","id":1501490,"title":"","content":"I'm still not really comfortable with how &quot;mainstream&quot; is being used as a short hand for, &quot;mainstream in English speaking cultures.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's even worse to me as we continue to see that the attempt of media hegemony in the Anglosphere has actually increased how much general audiences are turning towards entertainment from other cultures. South Korea, thanks to it's long term cultural exchange with the US after the Korean War, has really mastered making live-action entertainment that's still accessible to Western culture audiences. You don't need to actually be all that open minded to be a zombie fan and love the stuff coming out of Korean that's helping to revitalize the subgenre. Squid Game took off just fine, and people not getting it weren't missing the point because of a language barrier (since plenty of people have missed the same points when English language satires make them). Parasite and Minari both had massive critical acclaim and English language audiences came out in droves for them.<br /> <br /> Gen X, Millenials, and Zoomers are all used to watching stuff from other cultures. Gen X and older Millenials generally had the experiences of seeing how bad localization used to be and started actively pushing for less &quot;creative&quot; reinterpretations that changed things from the originals that didn't need changing (how we got the whole sub vs. dub wars). Was the American remake of Old Boy bad per se? Not really. But I've never met anyone that's watched the original and the American remake actually recommend watching the remake. If you really can't handle subtitles, the dub is still better than a remake that fails to actually do anything with the material to make it worth your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:09:54-08:00","id":1501491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream#post1501283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time believing that something like that will ever happen as most people would rather play video games and may not be willing to sit down and play a TTRPG, even if it is through an online platform. Many people these days don't even know what a TTRPG is.<br /> <br /> What about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that currently in regard to reach and popularity Vampire: the Masquerade (and also as well World of Darkness) are doing certainly good enough. The setting, the characters, the story, and also as well the themes, concepts, values, knowledge, topics, and ideas VtM contains are certainly: nicely attractive, very intricate, rather understandable, quite rich, and distinctly beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:56:03-08:00","id":1501502,"title":"","content":"First off, vampirism itself is not widely mainstream.<br /> <br /> It's a niche. Not everybody cares about stories of vampires.<br /> <br /> For people who does, VtM is a huge reference.<br /> <br /> And then, you have to combine people who likes vampires and people who play RPGs.<br /> <br /> The intersection of which is where you'll find VtM players.<br /> <br /> That's why you dont have a copy of the books on every households.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T11:31:56-08:00","id":1501552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's even worse to me as we continue to see that the attempt of media hegemony in the Anglosphere has actually increased how much general audiences are turning towards entertainment from other cultures. . </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I wouldn't attribute that to any sort of insidious hegemony but a wide array of factors.<br /> 1: Ever cheaper filming technology is really benefiting foreign cinema that previously struggled more with technological issues. Compare RRR to other Telugu films ten years ago.<br /> 2: The wealth of poorer regions is more often increasing while the western world stagnates and even regresses when considering cost of living. This means people of more developing nations are less occupied with surviving and now have the means to buy expensive things they don't need and can gleefully waste time consuming and creating a better market for domestically produced film and television.<br /> <br /> 3: I do think the culture war is worth mentioning. A few of my students have expressed dissatisfaction with some current western media; Netflix's apparent diversity policy and stuff like the Witcher (why does an IP that focuses on the nastiness of ignorance, racism and bigotry have the ethnic diversity of LA? People lose their shit if you've got pointy ears but nobody bats an eye seeing nilotic skin tones in a temperate continent that they've been living in for a thousand years. What kind of Eugenic program do they need to manage that? It's thematically anathema) and today people are making stuff like Velma, which, y'know, really is more of a statement than a TV show ( I haven't watched it, for all I know it could be good)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501490#post1501490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not really comfortable with how &quot;mainstream&quot; is being used as a short hand for, &quot;mainstream in English speaking cultures.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Europeans mostly agree on things and they're rarely primarily English speakers. Latin America and western/central Asia aren't that much different in my experience. (my job is literally having conversations for ESL purposes, I talk to everyone, though I'll admit it's almost entirely middle class people so there's some bias there)<br /> <br /> Where I live now, people don't give a shit. supplementing the paltry local offerings I see Turkish soap operas after slavic police dramas and American action comedies and Poirot . People repeatedly listen to Depeche mode and The Cranberries and slavic rap (They're not slavs). As I've said before, my partner's father in his 60's is a massive fan of Korean historicals. This is the global world we live in.<br /> .<br /> Indians are different and East Asians are often very different. Israelis have been interesting the few times I've had them. The number of Black African students I've had can be counted on one hand so I can't speak much for them. But yeah, If a film is massive in the west it's probably going to be massive almost everywhere else. A lot of values are universal and a lot of values are almost universal. People are more similar than different generally speaking (excluding the crazy ones)<br /> <br /> I think you need to relax man. We're not out to get you, and I can't really imagine the idea that the US is seriously trying to dominate the world by releasing media that largely highlight the flaws of US society. Then again my Job is to spread the anglo way so maybe I'm the enemy and you shouldn't listen to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T15:19:08-08:00","id":1501576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501552#post1501552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI wouldn't attribute that to any sort of insidious hegemony but a wide array of factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discounting the impact of how much global media is controlled (either from production all the way to viewers eyes, or just via distribution) by less than a dozen mega corporations split between the US, UK, Canada, and Australia seems like you're not really thinking about this very seriously. And that's not just TV shows and movies, it's also owning the companies that do entertainment news (not calling that journalism) and other promotional vendors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1: Ever cheaper filming technology is really benefiting foreign cinema that previously struggled more with technological issues. Compare RRR to other Telugu films ten years ago. </div> </div> </div>How, exactly, does that explain the explosion of Anime in the US in the 90s? Or how well K-dramas (which don't need RRR level effects) are doing on Netflix thanks to greater exposure via Parasite's big award showing and the commercial success of Squid Game?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: I do think the culture war is worth mentioning. </div> </div> </div>You never explain what this has to do with Anglosphere audiences becoming more open to entertainment from other cultures over the last three decades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, Europeans mostly agree on things and they're rarely primarily English speakers. </div> </div> </div>Is this a joke?<br /> <br /> [quote]...though I'll admit it's almost entirely middle class people so there's some bias there)[/qutoe]<br /> <br /> There's a huge amount of bias there, esp. in developing countries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where I live now, people don't give a shit. </div> </div> </div>About... what exactly? You're not talking to what I was saying at all.<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indians are different and East Asians are often very different. Israelis have been interesting the few times I've had them. The number of Black African students I've had can be counted on one hand so I can't speak much for them. </div> </div> </div>So you talk to everyone... while admitting that 5/8 of the world's population either doesn't fit with what you're saying, or you don't really know if they do or not?<br /> <br /> This is exactly why I dislike claiming &quot;mainstream&quot; can be stated universally instead of specifying what culture you're really talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yeah, If a film is massive in the west it's probably going to be massive almost everywhere else. A lot of values are universal and a lot of values are almost universal. People are more similar than different generally speaking (excluding the crazy ones) </div> </div> </div>This is demonstrably untrue. Besides basic things like government censorship (which is very strong in most countries regarding media, and not just &quot;different&quot; ones like China, try getting something released in Australia), cultural values frequently lead to disparate reactions to films. Huge box office returns in some parts of the world do not automatically mean global success.<br /> <br /> The increased trend in that direction isn't some sense of universal values, but that major studios have whole executive teams dedicated to adjusting the marketing and production budgets for films based on their perceived global appeal. When Disney decides something isn't going to work in China, they cut back on it's budget and write off that giant pool of sales. This then becomes self fulfilling as movies are predetermined to unappealing in some markets, and then aren't offered to those markets, and aren't aimed for global blockbuster status over films that executives feel can achieve that status.<br /> <br /> Lots of stuff that's wildly successful in the West never makes it to other markets because it never gets a chance. The correlation of Western success to global success you're making is backwards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you need to relax man. </div> </div> </div>Well, I need to relax after reading your post anyway. I have no idea how, &quot;I'm still not really comfortable with...&quot; was some statement of extreme agitation. We've interacted more than enough for you to know I don't mince words. And I certainly don't need your brand of armchair therapist that confuses being an ass with trying to state &quot;hard truths.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're not out to get you, and I can't really imagine the idea that the US is seriously trying to dominate the world by releasing media that largely highlight the flaws of US society. Then again my Job is to spread the anglo way so maybe I'm the enemy and you shouldn't listen to me. </div> </div> </div>I live in the US. The US media already has me.<br /> <br /> I also live in a country where one of our major parties regularly elects people that openly associate with people that espouse ideologies that involve me being murdered. So... yeah, I tend to be suspicious of people with power in this country.<br /> <br /> Of course &quot;media hegemony&quot; in the US isn't actually about the best interests of the US (most of the culture war is stoked by the media for profit), just the bottom line of a bunch of rich assholes.<br /> <br /> I have no idea if you're the &quot;enemy&quot; or not, but you don't really seem to want to engage with the realities of what we're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T16:58:18-08:00","id":1501582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501552#post1501552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't attribute that to any sort of insidious hegemony but a wide array of factors.<br /> 1: Ever cheaper filming technology is really benefiting foreign cinema that previously struggled more with technological issues. Compare RRR to other Telugu films ten years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true... India has a rich and lengthy film-history, be it in in Telugu or Hindi. There's no need for a benefactor at this point (and hasn't been for a while). Bollywood has been a thing for a while and Tollywood has been trying to catch up and a movie like RRR will certainly help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501552#post1501552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: The wealth of poorer regions is more often increasing while the western world stagnates and even regresses when considering cost of living. This means people of more developing nations are less occupied with surviving and now have the means to buy expensive things they don't need and can gleefully waste time consuming and creating a better market for domestically produced film and television.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has little to do with the thread but just wanted to point out that that's untrue. A quote from the 2023 Oxfam-report:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worldwide, only four cents in every tax dollar now comes from taxes on wealth. Half of the world\u2019s billionaires live in countries with no inheritance tax for direct descendants. They will pass on a $5 trillion tax-free treasure chest to their heirs, more than the GDP of Africa, which will drive a future generation of aristocratic elites. Rich people\u2019s income is mostly unearned, derived from returns on their assets, yet it is taxed on average at 18 percent, just over half as much as the average top tax rate on wages and salaries. </div> </div> </div>If you're looking for people whose wealth increases while doing nothing worthwhile look to the rich.<br /> <br /> And the rest of the report, you may wonder...? Just more of the usual... The rich have gotten richer, the poor have gotten poorer... Anyone not aware of this dynamic has been living under a rock for the past couple decades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501552#post1501552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3: I do think the culture war is worth mentioning. A few of my students have expressed dissatisfaction with some current western media; Netflix's apparent diversity policy and stuff like the Witcher (why does an IP that focuses on the nastiness of ignorance, racism and bigotry have the ethnic diversity of LA? People lose their shit if you've got pointy ears but nobody bats an eye seeing nilotic skin tones in a temperate continent that they've been living in for a thousand years. What kind of Eugenic program do they need to manage that? It's thematically anathema) and today people are making stuff like Velma, which, y'know, really is more of a statement than a TV show ( I haven't watched it, for all I know it could be good)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a superficial analysis might lead you to believe that. \u201cGo woke, go broke\u201d, that kind of thing. An easy analysis where you can shut your brain off and just start repeating phrases that fit within in an overly simplistic narrative.<br /> <br /> To make a long story short: A bunch of silly horseshit.<br /> <br /> Witcher: Blood Origins sucked ass. Velma sucks ass. Another show not mentioned here that I think fits this category is the new Willow TV show. It also is terrible. They obviously have aspirations of being \u201cwoke\u201d for fulfilling quotas of diversity. But it\u2019s superficial. Having homosexual characters never means plotting or storytelling \u00e0 la \u201clet\u2019s examine the experience of homosexuals in the 90s\u201d, it\u2019s just \u201cOh hey, that character\u2019s gay\u2026 isn\u2019t that something\u2026!\u201d. And that blandness is the norm for these aspirations to diversity. Because none of these shows are doing anything radical and/or interesting.<br /> <br /> The much bigger problem is that none of these shows are well written in a conventional sense. And what\u2019s even the point of doing identity-politics with having a homosexual character in the cast while writing horseshit for that character\u2026 not that these shows are doing any better with straight characters, of course, so maybe that was too much to ask.<br /> <br /> These are shows trying to seem appealing to certain groups and that\u2019s it. It\u2019s about getting people to watch shit. That\u2019s it. There\u2019s your grand conspiracy. Rather than politics the thing at the center of this is consumption-culture and micro-targeting. As long as you engage with the content and fit a category, all is fine. Doesn\u2019t matter why you do it. Everything\u2019s a product, everything\u2019s perishables. Consumption is everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T04:40:44-08:00","id":1501602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501582#post1501582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not true... India has a rich and lengthy film-history, be it in in Telugu or Hindi. There's no need for a benefactor at this point (and hasn't been for a while). Bollywood has been a thing for a while and Tollywood has been trying to catch up and a movie like RRR will certainly help.</div> </div> </div> </div> Was more a statement for media worldwide rather than just India. Given what masterpieces Ugandans could achieve with $200 I shudder to think how the world would change if they got more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Has little to do with the thread but just wanted to point out that that's untrue. A quote from the 2023 Oxfam-report:<br /> And the rest of the report, you may wonder...? Just more of the usual... The rich have gotten richer, the poor have gotten poorer... Anyone not aware of this dynamic has been living under a rock for the past couple decades.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Billionaires aren't the people. I suppose they do fund these things and have an outsized influence, but I'm talking about the 99% that consume these things and how it effects the world rather than just the social classes of a particular nation. The Average Brit is poorer even if certain parts of London are doing great, but the important thing is that in much of the world people can see their living conditions improve in real time. Things like the housing crises are almost purely a phenomenon of North America/Europe/Australia and other rich nations. Developing countries have their own particular problems, but in a lot of cases they're exploding with economic growth and genuine improvements to the quality of life for ordinary people, which translates to things like eating more meat, buying oversized TVs, and consuming pop culture.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, a superficial analysis might lead you to believe that. \u201cGo woke, go broke\u201d, that kind of thing. An easy analysis where you can shut your brain off and just start repeating phrases that fit within in an overly simplistic narrative.<br /> <br /> The much bigger problem is that none of these shows are well written in a conventional sense. And what\u2019s even the point of doing identity-politics with having a homosexual character in the cast while writing horseshit for that character\u2026 not that these shows are doing any better with straight characters, of course, so maybe that was too much to ask<br /> <br /> These are shows trying to seem appealing to certain groups and that\u2019s it. It\u2019s about getting people to watch shit. That\u2019s it. There\u2019s your grand conspiracy. Rather than politics the thing at the center of this is consumption-culture and micro-targeting. As long as you engage with the content and fit a category, all is fine. Doesn\u2019t matter why you do it. Everything\u2019s a product, everything\u2019s perishables. Consumption is everything. </div> </div> </div>That's exactly the issue: terrible products will be greenlit if they tick the right boxes, and the boxes must be ticked even if they compromise the integrity of the story. Meanwhile, politics is used to shield sub-par content. Don't like <i>The Woman King</i>? It must be because you're a racist sexist and your reviews shouldn't be on aggregate sites because you're not judging the film you're just outraged that someone made a film not about white men. Thus 99% love that film according to rotten tomatoes... because we're discounting all the people that don't. This is really offputting/confusing stuff if you're not in the anglosphere (especially if you're like, from west africa and actually know the history whitewashed by<i> The Woman king</i>), and I've yet to meet a Pole that appreciated whatever was done to satiate the &quot;modern audiences&quot; when adapting The Witcher. I realise there are genuine nutters out there who'll send hate purely because of someone's race in STAR WARS of all things, but it's offputting that so much alienating crap comes out nowadays and all &quot;valid&quot; reviews point to it being the greatest hotness.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501576#post1501576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You never explain what this has to do with Anglosphere audiences becoming more open to entertainment from other cultures over the last three decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing volume of foreign media<br /> Increasing quality of foreign media<br /> There is a decreased stigma towards &quot;geek&quot; culture in general.<br /> Hollywood being stupid as discussed prior.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is this a joke? </div> </div> </div>Not at all, at least in context. The first thing that has to be said is that people in the same country are rarely on the same page with one another, nevermind other countries. There are crazy people from every nation, so with that in mind a good chunk of people from France have more in common with many similar people from Poland than they do with many other French people. Northern europeans can generally be considered less friendly and tend to eat more potatoes while southern europeans are often very friendly and don't eat so many potatoes, but most differences are superficial. When we're discussing what kind of media people like, ultimately things like class, gender or personal interests are going to be significanly more important than nationality or native language.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 01-29-2023, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T08:13:07-08:00","id":1501615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501602#post1501602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given what masterpieces Ugandans could achieve with $200 I shudder to think how the world would change if they got more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except exposure is more important than more money to make films in this regard though. RRR isn't just that budgets in Tollywood have gotten bigger, but that they could push it to Western audiences on Netflix's main English language page instead of it only streaming in the foreign language section/on smaller and more local services. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose they do fund these things and have an outsized influence, but I'm talking about the 99% that consume these things and how it effects the world rather than just the social classes of a particular nation. </div> </div> </div>And this is where your middle-class heavy exposure bias is definitely showing. Most developing countries have a growing middle class... at the expense of worsening conditions for the lower classes. A small heavy consumer class that demands more prestige goods also means drowning out the &quot;cheaper&quot; media that everyone that wasn't filthy rich used to share.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't like <i>The Woman King</i>? It must be because you're a racist sexist and your reviews shouldn't be on aggregate sites because you're not judging the film you're just outraged that someone made a film not about white men. Thus 99% love that film according to rotten tomatoes... because we're discounting all the people that don't. </div> </div> </div>Now how needs to chill and stop being so conspiratorial?<br /> <br /> Rotten Tomatoes introduced a &quot;verified viewer&quot; review rating to cut down on review bombing: you need to scan your ticket/etc. to show that you actually bought the right to see the movie. While there's certainly a selection bias towards positive reviews (if you didn't like the movie you're much less likely to go through extra steps to say so on RT). They still have a tab for seeing what the aggregate of everyone that didn't get verified would do to the rankings.<br /> <br /> It is a bit odd that the unverified negative reviews complain heavily that the verified reviews didn't actually watch the movie or they wouldn't praise it so much... but the verified reviews are all from people that went through a step to prove they at least bought a ticket, while the unverified ones didn't.<br /> <br /> That doesn't exactly scream rigging over politics.<br /> <br /> Of course, you've also contradicted yourself here. The Women King was very successful in the West, but not as successful elsewhere (esp. west Africa)... precisely because of different cultural values and norms that are directly linked to location. In the Anglosphere where black and African stories are under-represented in media, there's more positivity towards telling those stories (is it fully historically accurate? Not really, but very few &quot;based on true story&quot; movies are). For people that have grown up in that part of Africa, where the vast majority of who they see in entertainment already looks like them? It's a completely different value judgement on the film.<br /> <br /> We saw the same thing with the live action Ghost in the Shell (to pick something a bit less controversial on how good of a movie it may or may not be). Japanese audiences generally didn't give a shit about casting non-Japanese characters because their lives are flooded with Japanese characters played by Japanese people. American audiences were much more put off by a white woman getting a Japanese woman's part because America has a long history of giving ethnic characters to white actors instead of giving actors from the right backgrounds a shot.<br /> <br /> Those are some of those values that don't mesh with the idea that stuff is more &quot;universal&quot; than not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Increasing volume of foreign media<br /> Increasing quality of foreign media<br /> There is a decreased stigma towards &quot;geek&quot; culture in general.<br /> Hollywood being stupid as discussed prior. </div> </div> </div>Which.. doesn't explain the culture wars point at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first thing that has to be said is that people in the same country are rarely on the same page with one another, nevermind other countries. </div> </div> </div>That's... the exact opposite of what you said. Which is it? Are Europeans basically one group that we don't have to respect differences between them, or not?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T20:06:24-08:00","id":1501659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream#post1501283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time believing that something like that will ever happen as most people would rather play video games and may not be willing to sit down and play a TTRPG, even if it is through an online platform. Many people these days don't even know what a TTRPG is.<br /> <br /> What about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in the '90's, V:tM was pretty main-stream; everyone in our group of friends knew of it. And it wasn't that we'd rather play video-games, we would RPG, then, when we got bored or a new game came out, we'd play video-games, like <i>Power Monger</i>, until we either got bored or one of our friends wanted to role-play their character. No big deal. And when we weren't playing V:tM to RPG, we'd play Cyberpunk:2020 or Dark Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T11:36:34-08:00","id":1501730,"title":"","content":"I mean, I don't think we'll go back to the days where it had a TV show and you could buy shirts and books at Hot Topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T11:58:08-08:00","id":1501735,"title":"","content":"Sadly those days seem to be a distant memory ZakRulz and maybe they will come back when the Entertainment industry go back to the basics of writing good stories with good characters that are well rounded and not carboard cutouts that are used to push a plot forward or whatnot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T14:56:44-08:00","id":1501746,"title":"","content":"There was never such a time. You're just letting a bias born of a highly curated selection of past works disguise that as long as entertainment has been an industry, the contemporary moment is always full of drek trying to maximize profit off of minimal work.<br /> <br /> Only a tiny fraction of each generation's creative output gets preserved and represented to subsequent generations. So only the best (even if that gets reevaluated at times) stuff is offered, making the past look like it was full of wonderful creativity and the present a miserable slog of hunting for needles in a haystack of bland shit. The reality is you're just seeing the work of other people finding those shit covered needles for you (and sometimes people going back to the shit pile because a needle should have gotten saved but wasn't, or tossing a bad needle back in where it belongs).<br /> <br /> The reason why there isn't a VtM TV show already is largely because Paradox made a bunch of decisions that devalued the brand to TV producers. It has nothing to do with some rose-colored glasses view of art history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T00:47:27-08:00","id":1501782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501746#post1501746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why there isn't a VtM TV show already is largely because Paradox made a bunch of decisions that devalued the brand to TV producers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, we are just ignoring <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115232/\" target=\"_blank\">Kindred: the Embraced</a> tv series which came out about 8 years before Bloodlines released?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T00:57:55-08:00","id":1501783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501746#post1501746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why there isn't a VtM TV show already is largely because Paradox made a bunch of decisions that devalued the brand to TV producers. It has nothing to do with some rose-colored glasses view of art history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its more than that vtm prior to v5 didn't have the brand value required to pull it off. V5 needed to bolster it to get that. The errors they've made set their objective further back rather than sabotaged something already doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-31-2023, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T01:00:02-08:00","id":1501784,"title":"","content":"There's a error where trying to edit your posts can get them locked as spam the forum team is trying to hammer out. Consider that means going back to clarify poor phrasing and typos isn't as simple as it used to be.<br /> <br /> Considering said show was referenced to the old show a few posts up, I think you can safely assume the &quot;new&quot; my post lacks between &quot;a&quot; and &quot;VtM.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T01:06:19-08:00","id":1501786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501783#post1501783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think its more than that vtm prior to v5 didn't have the brand value required to pull it off. V5 needed to bolster it to get that. The errors they've made set their objective further back rather than sabotaged something already doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The amount of hype easily built around the BL 2 announcement doesn't really support this.<br /> <br /> Also... in 2016 would you have believe there was any brand value in Castlevania to bush a highly successful Netflix show? How many people doubted Guardians of the Galaxy as a Marvel property to obscure for the MCU?<br /> <br /> The last 15 years is just full of examples of brands that don't seem to have strong value still working. Reviving relatively niche properties isn't as big of an obstacle as it used to seem. Dealing with a brand that's had a rough revival in a different medium first is a different issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T01:31:25-08:00","id":1501788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501786#post1501786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The amount of hype easily built around the BL 2 announcement doesn't really support this.<br /> <br /> Also... in 2016 would you have believe there was any brand value in Castlevania to bush a highly successful Netflix show? How many people doubted Guardians of the Galaxy as a Marvel property to obscure for the MCU?<br /> <br /> The last 15 years is just full of examples of brands that don't seem to have strong value still working. Reviving relatively niche properties isn't as big of an obstacle as it used to seem. Dealing with a brand that's had a rough revival in a different medium first is a different issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> possibly but dont actually know how it would have done. Game hype doesn't translate to market success or even quality or vice versa.<br /> <br /> Marvel has way more cultural clout thatn wod even during the 90s . Same to a lesser degree for castlevania<br /> <br /> And for every one of them we have 10 which went no where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-31-2023, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T04:31:38-08:00","id":1501802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501782#post1501782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, we are just ignoring <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115232/\" target=\"_blank\">Kindred: the Embraced</a> tv series which came out about 8 years before Bloodlines released?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I found it entertaining enough, but when we're talking about it's quality as an adaptation I'd put it right there with the Percy Jackson movies, which I also found entertaining. Inspired by, not based on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T08:49:11-08:00","id":1501815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501788#post1501788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> possibly but dont actually know how it would have done. Game hype doesn't translate to market success or even quality or vice versa.<br /> <br /> Marvel has way more cultural clout that wod even during the 90s . Same to a lesser degree for castlevania<br /> <br /> And for every one of them we have 10 which went no where.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not making any predictions on quality here. Just trying to make the case that to a large extent &quot;obscure franchise you haven't thought about in years,&quot; is actually a better place for a brand to be to try to expand into transmedia products than, &quot;revive brand that's been struggling even it its original media form, and flailing in others.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T09:42:19-08:00","id":1501817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501815#post1501815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not making any predictions on quality here. Just trying to make the case that to a large extent &quot;obscure franchise you haven't thought about in years,&quot; is actually a better place for a brand to be to try to expand into transmedia products than, &quot;revive brand that's been struggling even it its original media form, and flailing in others.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand but my counterpoint is that I consider this isnt a particularly strong position to launch a franchise for even framed in best context it has been done but as a historical trend i wouldn't recommend it. Setting your sites at some multi media empire I'd putting the cart before the horse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-31-2023, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T09:51:10-08:00","id":1501818,"title":"","content":"Is there such a thing as a strong position though? We've seen so many failures from established franchises trying to get shows or movies or video games (even when they've had success in those areas in the past!) it feels like - as far as brands are concerned - there's basically just weak and weaker positions, as most branded transmedia attempts produce more duds than hits.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, the only &quot;strong&quot; position is to be such a huge brand that even if yu release a bunch of duds, enough people pay to watch because it's such a big brand,that your investors at least break even and can be convinced to keep going (basically what's happening with DC).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T12:19:17-08:00","id":1501826,"title":"","content":"I would argue that VtM was mainstream for a good part of the early 90s. It has definitely fallen out of favor as the IP languished between CCP and Paradox for years. The general vibe of the game has kind of lost its steam too. Could swing back around as the general populace gets more doomer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27749-welard","name":"Welard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T00:56:44-08:00","id":1501854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501818#post1501818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there such a thing as a strong position though? We've seen so many failures from established franchises trying to get shows or movies or video games (even when they've had success in those areas in the past!) it feels like - as far as brands are concerned - there's basically just weak and weaker positions, as most branded transmedia attempts produce more duds than hits.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, the only &quot;strong&quot; position is to be such a huge brand that even if yu release a bunch of duds, enough people pay to watch because it's such a big brand,that your investors at least break even and can be convinced to keep going (basically what's happening with DC).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...yes? or at least theirs no universal principle for success. But theirs factors to nudge it in your favour. Coming in with a strong entrenched fanbase and an consistent idea of product is genrally a good groundwork. It also makes you more appealing to possible investors since you are effectively asking for a certain degree of good faith.<br /> <br /> For example If i was a suit id be more inclined towards twilight in 2007 as a pitch as it looks more likely to succeed with an established fandom, clear large scale momentum and Well established concept than wod with stunted development, increasingly fractured fanbase (which the developers might even have a degree of antipathy towards) which doesn't even seem to like it's own concepts now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-01-2023, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T09:03:01-08:00","id":1501873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Welard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501826#post1501826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that VtM was mainstream for a good part of the early 90s. It has definitely fallen out of favor as the IP languished between CCP and Paradox for years. The general vibe of the game has kind of lost its steam too.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting question is - do <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> and <i>Vampire: the Requiem</i> directly and distinctly contribute to the popularity and good image and positive reception of <i>V:tM</i> as an excellent, complex, positive, and extensive example and work of vampire fiction?<br /> <br /> Of course it has to be noted and emphasized that <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is to a considerable and significant extent developed, created, planned, outlined, and written as a setting, a backdrop, and a framework for a wonderful, curious, and interesting role-playing game. Which as one of it's main features has the intricate atmosphere and the many varied themes, and also as well the nice, good, and interesting heroes, characters, villians, and protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T09:25:40-08:00","id":1501874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501873#post1501873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting question is - do <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> and <i>Vampire: the Requiem</i> directly and distinctly contribute to the popularity and good image and positive reception of <i>V:tM</i> as an excellent, complex, positive, and extensive example and work of vampire fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Chronicles of Darkness by itself just confuses outsiders trying to learn about World of Darkness. I can't even put a number on how many times I've seen people confused about the whole CofD/nWoD and WoD/oWoD situation. VtR is practically unknown compared to VtM.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T09:29:02-08:00","id":1501875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501873#post1501873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting question is - do <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> and <i>Vampire: the Requiem</i> directly and distinctly contribute to the popularity and good image and positive reception of <i>V:tM</i> as an excellent, complex, positive, and extensive example and work of vampire fiction?<br /> <br /> Of course it has to be noted and emphasized that <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is to a considerable and significant extent developed, created, planned, outlined, and written as a setting, a backdrop, and a framework for a wonderful, curious, and interesting role-playing game. Which as one of it's main features has the intricate atmosphere and the many varied themes, and also as well the nice, good, and interesting heroes, characters, villians, and protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. I actually think that attempts to add mass appeal to the WoD are the things harming it the most. Paradox seems to be killing of CofD anyway and its for the best. Vigil and Forsaken are cool mechanically, but please give me back my grunge edgelord game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27749-welard","name":"Welard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T10:58:52-08:00","id":1501881,"title":"","content":"The CofD being killed off isn't for the best, even for the WoD's brand. It just makes Paradox look worse as a company to partner with.<br /> <br /> There was a significant period of time when the head developer for Apocalypse 20th and Forsaken was the same person. It was a great time because you had someone directly making sure each Werewolf game was doing its own thing,and you could get books for either as you wanted. Both WoD and CofD coexisting was one of the best times to be a fan of either game. Cancelling the CofD doesn't increase the ability to make WoD books, and isn't going to make CofD fans suddenly buy WoD stuff (in fact generally it will cause the opposite).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T11:12:03-08:00","id":1501889,"title":"","content":"Lets us never mention Twilight in these hallowed halls and I'm still trying to wrap my head around why it became popular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T04:10:56-08:00","id":1501941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501889#post1501889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets us never mention Twilight in these hallowed halls and I'm still trying to wrap my head around why it became popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>What eludes you? A blank page put between a handsome brooding man who's really not that bad and a hunky native man who'll love you like a puppy? How could this possibly be popular targeted towards the teenage girl demographic?<br /> I'm not sure if it was Ironic or not but as a teenage boy I found the movies to be an enjoyable watch. Yeah, sparkling is a little silly and there's some other questionable stuff there, but I think the hate directed towards it more often doesn't often come from the best of places. Hating popular things/Jealousy/bandwagoning /Pretentiousness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-ZrvflNZPCM\" data-code=\"-ZrvflNZPCM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-ZrvflNZPCM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This scene is and will always be gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T11:31:04-08:00","id":1501964,"title":"","content":"Basically. Twilight is a YA romance that happens to use supernatural characters, and YA romance books mostly go under the radar, but when one (or even better a series) lands? They land huge. YA and women audience focused romance fiction is a huge business that for some reason people that never engage with it don't seem to realize.<br /> <br /> What gets misunderstood on forums like this one, that are focused on supernatural horror first, is that these sorts of stories aren't meant to appeal to hardcore supernatural horror fans. Back in ye olden days when Buffy came out, the WoD community was immensely negative towards a woman that hunts vampires falls for the one vampire with a soul romance drama. Almost all the critiques weren't about anything wrong with Buffy doing what Buffy is trying to do (and there's plenty there) just like the general view of Twilight around here isn't about what's wrong with it for what its trying to do. They're not franchises about trying to do what VtM does. They got popular knowing how to be popular to the audiences that wanted what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T11:35:25-08:00","id":1501965,"title":"","content":"I want to write a dumb YA book and get rich...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T11:39:35-08:00","id":1501966,"title":"","content":"I like Twilight. I don\u2019t see a problem with liking books like Twilight and Hunger Games and also liking games like VtM too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T12:19:24-08:00","id":1501969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501965#post1501965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to write a dumb YA book and get rich...</div> </div> </div> </div>Better find out what the target audience likes now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T14:20:37-08:00","id":1501980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501874#post1501874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all. Chronicles of Darkness by itself just confuses outsiders trying to learn about World of Darkness. I can't even put a number on how many times I've seen people confused about the whole CofD/nWoD and WoD/oWoD situation. VtR is practically unknown compared to VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sadly have to agree. When I asked as a newbie I only got told en masse I should watch out not fall for the bad WoD as in nWoD is just an attempt to create a better product but that is actually worse then the original game that killed the original masterpiece for this &quot;Verschlimmbesserungen&quot; (german for improvements that made it actually worse)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T20:34:46-08:00","id":1502002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1501969#post1501969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better find out what the target audience likes now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear the kids like twitch, fortnite and iskeai anime. So just ask an AI to write a story about a twitch streamer who gets isekai-d into fortnite and then polish it up. Boom, easiest million dollars you'll ever make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T21:00:21-08:00","id":1502005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502002#post1502002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hear the kids like twitch, fortnite and iskeai anime. So just ask an AI to write a story about a twitch streamer who gets isekai-d into fortnite and then polish it up. Boom, easiest million dollars you'll ever make.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then thanks to the current economy, that million dollars will almost buy you a house, one year of taxes, and maybe a happy meal. Then you are right back at where you started, except you can't afford the property tax the following year.<br /> <br /> Sadly, that the optimistic outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T01:48:52-08:00","id":1502013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502005#post1502005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then thanks to the current economy, that million dollars will almost buy you a house, one year of taxes, and maybe a happy meal. Then you are right back at where you started, except you can't afford the property tax the following year.<br /> <br /> Sadly, that the optimistic outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>You guys have to pay tax to the house which you own and where live in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T03:30:17-08:00","id":1502016,"title":"","content":"Technically, in the US, you pay a property tax for any real estate you own. How rate of taxation is based on the value of the property, and a lot with a house on it is worth a lot more than an empty lot with some weeds growing on it.<br /> <br /> This is, quite stupidly, the primary method for paying for primary and secondary education in public schools here. Which exists pretty much exclusively to ensure the rich stay rich and the poor stay poor because poor communities own less property, and what property they do own is worth less so is taxed less, and thus their schools get less funding.<br /> <br /> This has minimal impact on any of the topics at hand though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T04:36:05-08:00","id":1502018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502013#post1502013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You guys have to pay tax to the house which you own and where live in?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to virtually every economist ever it's better and more ethical to mostly tax land value rather than income, but unfortunately such ideas came at a time where everyone in charge had significant amounts of valuable land. Related: Vampires care the most about land. <br /> <br /> VAT is a tax on the poor... and tourists, so it's not so bad in some places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T04:56:05-08:00","id":1502020,"title":"","content":"Most capitalist economists would probably mean that it's better to tax wealth than income, because wealth hoarding locks value out of the economy. Property taxes are one of the few remaining wealth taxes in the US (we used to tax way more types of wealth), and to replace that we tax income and consumption far more than makes any lick of sense.<br /> <br /> Likewise, vampires don't really care about land itself. Vampires don't buy dirt patches just to increase how much land they have. They care about land the same reason land was the main source of measuring wealth for most of human history: you can't have human civilization without land and putting land to use. Land means agriculture to feed people, housing to home them, and so on. Sufficiently prosperous land can maintain settlements that eventually grow into cities, and that means a high population concentration and increased human nocturnal activity for vampires to use for feeding. Land is the key form of wealth, because all other forms of wealth are meaningless if you can't trade them for stuff that comes from the land. For vampires that's blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T16:59:33-08:00","id":1502064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502016#post1502016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, in the US, you pay a property tax for any real estate you own. How rate of taxation is based on the value of the property, and a lot with a house on it is worth a lot more than an empty lot with some weeds growing on it.<br /> <br /> This is, quite stupidly, the primary method for paying for primary and secondary education in public schools here. Which exists pretty much exclusively to ensure the rich stay rich and the poor stay poor because poor communities own less property, and what property they do own is worth less so is taxed less, and thus their schools get less funding.<br /> <br /> This has minimal impact on any of the topics at hand though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is that there is another level to property tax and real estate value, depending on where the property is. Namely that the tax rate can be locked in at the time of purchase and the sale price. So a house purchased say in the 1940s would pay around $500 a year in property taxes, but if that same property was sold to a new owner the tax rate would be modernized and thus be around $4,500 a year. The loophole being that if you inherit the property from a family member, then you inherit that original tax bracket. All of this depends on local laws of course.<br /> <br /> As far as the rich staying rich and the poor staying poor, it would be more accurate to say that the system penalizes people who don't set down roots. If your grandparents purchase a house and pay off the mortgage, then your parents inherit it and are able to save money because there isn't a mortgage to pay. By the time the grandchildren inherit the house they might have to do some expensive renovations, but they can easily turn the house into a rental to generate money. All the while benefiting from the grandparents property original tax rate. All of this goes away if the offspring sells the house to finance other things.<br /> <br /> From a vampire perspective this gets very interesting because the farther back in time you purchase property, the cheaper it is to pay for. With an unlimited lifespan a vampire can use banking and property loopholes in ways mortals can only dream of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T17:44:05-08:00","id":1502067,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really change the &quot;rich stay rich&quot; much, because you need to meet certain levels of financial success to buy a house, pay off a mortgage, and even more so if the area is desirable enough to have multiple generations live there. Poor people can feel like they've set down roots, because they've lived in the same town for generations, but if they never had the money to obtain land-based wealth, none of what you're talking about kicks in.<br /> <br /> Also, whether property taxes are grandfathered in like that varies highly by state, esp. compared to how public school funding is determined (which also impacts property values if you want to leverage a grandfathered low property tax to use a house as a source of collateral or income), as does how inheritance taxes get calculated in states/areas with grandfathered property taxes vs. ones that don't. If you live in a state with grandfathered property taxes, but high inheritance taxes that are based on the current value of the house, you can easily get taxed far more for taking your parent's house over than you'll ever save in property taxes.<br /> <br /> The problem for vampires trying to take advantage of this, is that they have far easier ways to accumulate wealth that doesn't involve regularly faking their own deaths and being their own descendants (which has gotten much harder), they can achieve all sorts of savings because their budgets don't have to account for nearly as much as living people, and proximity to reliable blood sources is always going to make a bigger difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T19:18:01-08:00","id":1502071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502067#post1502067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't really change the &quot;rich stay rich&quot; much, because you need to meet certain levels of financial success to buy a house, pay off a mortgage, and even more so if the area is desirable enough to have multiple generations live there. Poor people can feel like they've set down roots, because they've lived in the same town for generations, but if they never had the money to obtain land-based wealth, none of what you're talking about kicks in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice most of your examples are &quot;they feel like&quot; rather than they actually did x, y, or z. There is a big difference between achieving something and feeling entitled to it without actually accomplishing it. Hence why in my example the grandparents worked their entire lives to eventually buy and pay off their house and only the following generations reap the benefits of it. In our modern world there is a heavier focus on building something of value for oneself rather than the future generations, who are in turn expected to work for most of their lives to add to that accomplishment for their descendants. <br /> <br /> A cynical interpretation would be that modern people are too focused on the &quot;screw you, I got mine&quot; mentality to understand the value of longer-term benefits or in some cases how money &amp; power actually work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502067#post1502067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem for vampires trying to take advantage of this, is that they have far easier ways to accumulate wealth that doesn't involve regularly faking their own deaths and being their own descendants (which has gotten much harder), they can achieve all sorts of savings because their budgets don't have to account for nearly as much as living people, and proximity to reliable blood sources is always going to make a bigger difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively rather than faking their deaths, a vampire just creates a holding company to own all the properties. Which means no faking your death or creating new identities and still retain the original property tax rates.<br /> <br /> Truthfully this is an excellent example of where game design development could help things. Consider if each vampire who starts to accumulate property or businesses, they need someone to do the day to day management. Most people would just have a ghoul boss, but in truth given enough time you could develop ghoul families whose entire existence grew out of being management staff for the same vampire over the centuries or even millennia. Kind of like in the Exalted setting where each Celestial exalt in the first age more or less had an entire Dragon-Blooded Gens assigned to them.<br /> <br /> VtM is mostly designed to be a Lost Boys street level game, but the fluff always talks about how an established vampire has this or that level of power. But when you go into the logistics of how to run that sort of setup, the game mechanics don't support it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T10:13:45-08:00","id":1502216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502071#post1502071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively rather than faking their deaths, a vampire just creates a holding company to own all the properties. Which means no faking your death or creating new identities and still retain the original property tax rates.<br /> <br /> Truthfully this is an excellent example of where game design development could help things. Consider if each vampire who starts to accumulate property or businesses, they need someone to do the day to day management. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals and various mundane and normal establishments, families, churches, chapters, groups, clubs, and organisations could be controlled, directed, exploited, and influenced in many and ways and through various capabilities and methods to store, hide, assess, safekeep, and possiblty expand and develop material resources and monetary wealth of a Vampiress.<br /> <br /> For that matter, to at least a moderate and significant extent this could be said in regard assuring, safeguarding, diversifyng and expanding wealth, riches, funds, and resources of other (than Vampires who are Kindred) Undead / Deathless / Vampiric magical persons and supernatural beings. For instance this can also apply to at least some extent in regard to wealth and resources of a Setite Ghoul, or a Giovanni Ghoul, a Tremere Ghoul, or a Malkavian Ghoul.<br /> <br /> And all the same in regard to Revenants. It is clear and most likely that Obertus Revenants and Grimaldi Revenants can plan, choose, decide, spend, and manage her or his assets, riches, funds, money, and resources using clearly defined intricate positive, subtle, interesting, careful, and efficient methods, capabilities, and approaches.<br /> <br /> And also of course the gathering, handling, and managing of funds, wealth, or resources can definitely come with an optimistic, defined, good and distinct outlook and attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T14:04:12-08:00","id":1502237,"title":"","content":"I'm really late to the party so I apologize if I'm repeating something already said, but I thought V:tM WAS mainstream. I remember seeing LARPs covered on the news, conventions featured on 48 Hours (news show like 60 Minutes), and of course, videogames like Redemption and Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Fifteen to seventeen years ago they had a TV SERIES, on FOX. Granted, it only lasted one season, and for some reason changed the name to Kindred: the Embrace, but it had Ventrue, Nosferatu, and even an Assamite in one of the last episodes (I didn't even hear about V:tM until after the show ended).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what your definition of Mainstream is, but V:tM comes as close as I can think of... Without, you know, Hasbro buying it up like Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 02-05-2023, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T14:45:55-08:00","id":1502244,"title":"","content":"VtM was mainstream in the past tense of &quot;used to be.&quot; It fell out of that in the mid '00s: CCP's WoD MMO fell into development hell, the nWoD/CofD change over struggled with the core fans base and didn't lead to the CofD getting support for mainstream products, and it was a generally bad time for the RPG industry as a whole. As a note, the old TV show came out over 26 years ago, not 16. It was also... not good. Pretty much the only thing it had going for it was the main character, who's actor tragically died the year the show came out. Had that not happened, Fox might have kept the show going in hopes of retooling it to play to its strengths, but unfortunately that never got a chance to happen.<br /> <br /> Where VtM was in 2002 is vastly different from where VtM was in 2022. Two decades is plenty of time for things to fall out of the mainstream and into niche or cult status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T19:04:01-08:00","id":1502268,"title":"","content":"Yeah, whatever cultural cache VtM had back in the early 00s has largely been spent over the two decades since the game ended. The 20th Anniversary Edition helped to rekindle its cult following, sure. But if it served to repair some of the broken base, V5 only broken the base in new and exciting ways. Nor did that new edition succeed in really propelling VtM to new popular attention, despite cross-collaboration with the likes of Critical Role. Nor have big attempts to establish it within the gaming space before or after V5 succeeded. Whether it's the MMO that fell to development hell, the Bloodlines sequel that still hasn't materialized and seems no closer to arriving, or the narrative games that seemed to garner more controversy than attention.<br /> <br /> The original Bloodlines seems to be the only lasting legacy among most people who aren't in the tabletop space.<br /> <br /> It's worth observing that within the big controversy over D&amp;D's OGL, and the resulting mass examination of TTRPG alternatives to that system, you don't see many people talking about VtM. Plenty talking about Pathfinder, Call of Cthulhu, and the Old School Renaissance. But scarce little, from what I've observed, about Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say VtM is &quot;dead&quot; (no pun intended). But I wouldn't say its cultural penetration is growing. Not by a long shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T20:02:54-08:00","id":1502276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502268#post1502268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth observing that within the big controversy over D&amp;D's OGL, and the resulting mass examination of TTRPG alternatives to that system, you don't see many people talking about VtM. Plenty talking about Pathfinder, Call of Cthulhu, and the Old School Renaissance. But scarce little, from what I've observed, about Vampire: The Masquerade..</div> </div> </div> </div>Another factor of this is that the WoD community at large, and to some extent, material in the franchise itself, has somesort of undeserved &quot;superiority complex&quot; toward DnD. Stuff like the criticization of certain playstyles being &quot;too DnD&quot; or doing &quot;X is capeshit/trenchcoat katana&quot; is prevalent throughout WoD. And the series as of late is going down the path where only one style of play is acceptable and nothing else. Either you like playing as Anarch Neonate and nothing else, or you're basically out of here if you don't want to homebrew every little thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T09:11:52-08:00","id":1502694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502268#post1502268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, whatever cultural cache VtM had back in the early 00s has largely been spent over the two decades since the game ended. The 20th Anniversary Edition helped to rekindle its cult following, sure. But if it served to repair some of the broken base, V5 only broken the base in new and exciting ways. Nor did that new edition succeed in really propelling VtM to new popular attention, despite cross-collaboration with the likes of Critical Role. Nor have big attempts to establish it within the gaming space before or after V5 succeeded. Whether it's the MMO that fell to development hell, the Bloodlines sequel that still hasn't materialized and seems no closer to arriving, or the narrative games that seemed to garner more controversy than attention.<br /> <br /> The original Bloodlines seems to be the only lasting legacy among most people who aren't in the tabletop space.<br /> <br /> It's worth observing that within the big controversy over D&amp;D's OGL, and the resulting mass examination of TTRPG alternatives to that system, you don't see many people talking about VtM. Plenty talking about Pathfinder, Call of Cthulhu, and the Old School Renaissance. But scarce little, from what I've observed, about Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say VtM is &quot;dead&quot; (no pun intended). But I wouldn't say its cultural penetration is growing. Not by a long shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the first step towards something like regaining some momentum even just in the TTRPG sphere would be to take advantage of the release of the SRD 5.1 under Creative Commons to do a \u201cVtM5e\u201d (as in VtM as expressed using D&amp;D5e mechanics vs. V5).<br /> <br /> The fact is that in the present zeitgeist D&amp;D5e has been the gateway to ttrpgs for an entire generation and there are whole groups out there who aren\u2019t interested in looking at anything that doesn\u2019t use something close to its style of mechanics (a lot has been done on the margins\u2026 see the fan produced Star Wars 5e).<br /> <br /> D&amp;D5e itself has so little actual mechanical spine to it that it\u2019d mostly be a matter of figuring out how you want the archetypes to fit into its structure (ex. I\u2019d be inclined towards the \u201craces\u201d being the Clans providing minor buff and clan weakness, then abusing the multiclassing rules such that the \u201cclasses\u201d would be the discipline paths (and run say only 5 levels) and you start by default at level 3\u2026 D&amp;D backgrounds becomes packages of VtM\u2019s backgrounds\u2026 Feats are the equivalent of merits or not used in favor of only ASIs).<br /> <br /> Would it be something anyone here is particularly interested in? Probably not. But only appealing to those already here is just preaching to the choir, it\u2019s not reaching anyone outside the already existing sphere you\u2019d need to again make VtM mainstream.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T09:33:23-08:00","id":1502695,"title":"","content":"It was already mainstream when I was playing in the nineties. The real question might be if it can regain its mainstream status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T09:47:30-08:00","id":1502696,"title":"","content":"I think some of that's natural. There's no right way to play VTM, but if you play it like DnD... well, like, neither the fluff nor mechanics encourage that, but as most players go with what they know... <br /> IDK, I started DnD and Vampire at roughly the same time so I didn't have the idea in my head that I needed to solve my problems mano a mano. I read the core book and zeroed in on the Ventrue, Malkavians and Tremere, because at the time these were the clans that aligned with my idea of a vampire in a modern setting (the Toreador didn't interest me, and I thought the nosferatu might be hard for a first time play) but a lot of players with DnD backgrounds/the need to be a badass B-line towards Gangrel and Brujah stereotypes and like... they can be interesting but like... we've got a masquerade to worry about. I'm struggling trying to play 3d chess here but these other players are re-enacting <i>Fast and the Furious</i>. Nowadays I pride myself on the ability to play anything but it's quite understandable that Vampire players have strong preferences when it comes to the tone of the game. VTM can be a high stakes political drama, gritty noire, slapstick action comedy, a romantic escapade, or god forbid a &quot;personal horror&quot; among other things. In DnD the tone is like, 80% on the GM and people with different ideas can easily come to a consensus, but in vampire your own character's personal story is usually more important than whatever the ST gives you and so it can be more frustrating when other players undermine the tone you want. Thus, VTM players become elitist control freaks. <br /> <br /> Also, like, our views on the modern world will be very different: Player A might assume most police are noble and hyper-competent, player B might assume police are bad but still competent enough to worry about. Player C thinks of police as mobs to kill. This and many other politically minded ideas will shape how we approach any game set in the modern world. DnD doesn't really have this problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T11:49:51-08:00","id":1502703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502694#post1502694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the first step towards something like regaining some momentum even just in the TTRPG sphere would be to take advantage of the release of the SRD 5.1 under Creative Commons to do a \u201cVtM5e\u201d (as in VtM as expressed using D&amp;D5e mechanics vs. V5).</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really seem likely to work.<br /> <br /> First, there's a d20 based WoD game out there already made during the 3.X days. While not a flop, Monte Cooke's WoD is more of a novelty item than a serious pull for D&amp;D focused players to look at the WoD. If it didn't work during the first OGL boom, what would make it more appealing now?<br /> <br /> Second, there's a rather large push back against using the OGL that's managed to hit beyond RPG insiders and people that are into the hobby way more than playing D&amp;D because that's what people are playing. The recent events around the OGL has seen a major upswing in people looking for other options. While d20 clones like Pathfinder are going to snag the lion's share of that, it's probably the biggest dent in the public perception that &quot;RPG = D&amp;D&quot; since the height of the WoD's 90s era prominence. We're seeing a lot of community support for moving away from WotC run SRDs and towards things like ORC or just doing your own d20 inspired system (like Onyx20 is going to be starting with Pugmire).<br /> <br /> Third, but closely related to the second point there, is that we've seen a slow but incremental level of success of non-d20 inspired systems getting to wider audiences. One of the biggest drivers of this is that companies looking to license out their IPs to make RPGs are increasing looking at a wider variety of systems. Twenty years ago, everyone wanted an OGL d20 game for their IP... and it mostly lead to a lot of duds. We're seeing a lot more success in RPGs of existing properties partially because companies are being savvier about shopping for systems that are more likely to appeal to their target audience. There's an ever increasing recognition that &quot;non-D&amp;D brand with D&amp;D rules doesn't get you D&amp;D sales&quot; and that sales are better with a system that works of people that want your brand's RPG than trying to force into the d20 mold.<br /> <br /> The big problem for trying to get back to the WoD's former glory, is that space is more crowded now. It used to be D&amp;D, then WoD in a distance second, and then everyone else way behind that in public awareness. There are a lot more companies in the &quot;never going to be WotC, but still big enough a lot of non-hardcore gamers have heard of us,&quot; zone. The WoD needs to stand out in that space again, not try to latch on to a licensing scheme everyone else in the same space is fleeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T23:19:03-08:00","id":1502734,"title":"","content":"Also, trying to make an adaptation of VtM in D&amp;D 5e would require so much work to capture how VtM plays, you're basically making a new system that vaguely works like 5e. Which is not only a lot of labor on your end, but also asking just as much from a current 5e player to learn as just learning VtM.<br /> <br /> There's a sort of dead end thinking that arises when folks start reflexively trying to create a compromise between two things, when you're just better off trying to sell people on the other thing you actually want to sell them.<br /> <br /> Plus, 5e is hardly the smoothest transition in regards for adapting another game. GURPS was doing WoD adaptations basically from the beginning, precisely because GURPS is designed to be a modular system you can slot anything into. (I have problems with the GURPS system, which is why I bounced off it, but modularity is not one of them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T01:00:18-08:00","id":1502737,"title":"","content":"Using 5e for vampire's a terrible idea. 5e has a very streamlined skill system, either you have something or you don't. 5e is more about powers and abilities than skills. Vampire is more about skills than powers and most powers use skills. I think VTMs stronger for not using a class system (clans are maybe a &quot;soft&quot; class system but you could easily make a Ventrue who plays like a nosferatu).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T08:07:28-08:00","id":1502748,"title":"","content":"As I said, I doubted the idea would be very popular here, but \u201cpopular here\u201d was never the intent of the suggestion. If \u201cpopular here\u201d was enough to achieve mainstream notice we wouldn\u2019t be discussing what it would take to make VtM mainstream again here.<br /> <br /> Also, the OGL is now irrelevant because SRD5.1 is now under the irrevocable Creative Commons by Attribution 4.0 License. There is literally nothing Hasbro/WotC can do to revoke it.<br /> <br /> Even with the OGL debacle (which the complete surrender by WotC including putting SRD5.1 under CC-by-4.0 license basically ended with most of the DDB subscribers reactivating their subscriptions) D&amp;D5E has orders of magnitude more reach than VtM (on the order of $150 million in revenue last year).<br /> <br /> Yes, an adaptation of VtM using SRD5.1 as the base wouldn\u2019t be for virtually anyone here, it would be to extend the reach and awareness of it into a demographic that presently barely even knows VtM exists.<br /> <br /> If the goal is \u201cmake VtM mainstream\u201d then you need to preach beyond the choir and, to extend the metaphor, as any good evangelist knows, if you want to reach people you have to start with a message they can understand from where they\u2019re at.<br /> <br /> Yes, true believers will always find such messages insipid and lacking\u2026 but the message isn\u2019t FOR them and you can\u2019t grow without converts\u2026 and since it\u2019s not intended to replace, but as outreach it would certainly be less divisive than the X20/X5 matter has been (i.e. intended for a different audience entirely).<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re happy with things as they are in their present niche then clearly there is no need for any such outreach, a trickle of converts willing to fully buy in and brought in by existing members will keep things going well enough. But maintaining the niche was not the topic of the thread and so I answered the topic.<br /> <br /> The answer is, if you want to make VtM mainstream then you need to grow its audience enough for others to take notice of it and want to get involved with it.<br /> <br /> Paramount didn\u2019t make a D&amp;D-branded movie vs. a generic fantasy setting they wouldn\u2019t need to pay licensing for for no reason. They made it because the brand makes $150 million a year off 20% of its users buying the content and they believe they can profit from that brand recognition.<br /> <br /> No one\u2019s going to make a VtM movie or tv series (vs. a generic vampire series) if they don\u2019t think the brand recognition has value. No third party is beating down the door to use the IP in their own video games. And no one will until the brand improves its reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T15:05:04-08:00","id":1502774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502748#post1502748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, I doubted the idea would be very popular here, but \u201cpopular here\u201d was never the intent of the suggestion. If \u201cpopular here\u201d was enough to achieve mainstream notice we wouldn\u2019t be discussing what it would take to make VtM mainstream again here.<br /> ...<br /> If you\u2019re happy with things as they are in their present niche then clearly there is no need for any such outreach, a trickle of converts willing to fully buy in and brought in by existing members will keep things going well enough. But maintaining the niche was not the topic of the thread and so I answered the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty cheap rhetoric.<br /> <br /> You're basically deflecting all criticism of your post because you purposefully made it sound like your post would only be critiqued because we're not D&amp;D fans (how do you know what else everyone here likes or dislikes anyway?).<br /> <br /> Your &quot;suggestion&quot; has to stand on it's own merits. It's not good just because it elicited negative reactions here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The answer is, if you want to make VtM mainstream then you need to grow its audience enough for others to take notice of it and want to get involved with it. </div> </div> </div>There is zero evidence to suggest doing VtM with the SRD 5.1 will accomplish this. Paizo, who's whole brand is &quot;D&amp;D but better,&quot; isn't bothering to stick with SRD 5.1 and is still going through with their own system that doesn't rely on WotC's corporate whims. Why should anyone else think SRD 5.1 is the way to popularity when the company most suited to gain a bigger audience in the current gaming climate isn't doing that?<br /> <br /> Your suggestion <b>does not explain how this will expand audiences</b> because it doesn't explain why anyone will want to play &quot;VtM shoved into SRD 5.1 rules.&quot; It offers no examples of this working. It offers no counters to all the times it has failed past attempts. It doesn't address all the industry professionals ignoring this exact option for their own games. How do you know better than Paizo, or Green Ronin, or Onyx Path, or Games Workshop, or Fantasy Flight Games, or Modiphius, or Fria Ligan? Why are all of them doing not this? What do you think you know that they don't? Why should Paradox listen to you instead of looking at all of them?<br /> <br /> Are all of those companies also just &quot;the choir&quot; too biased to see the greatness of your suggestion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one\u2019s going to make a VtM movie or tv series (vs. a generic vampire series) if they don\u2019t think the brand recognition has value. No third party is beating down the door to use the IP in their own video games. And no one will until the brand improves its reach. </div> </div> </div>Have you read the whole thread? Do you honestly think we don't know this?<br /> <br /> This isn't the question. The question is how Paradox can actually dig themselves out of the hole they dug themselves after five years of not doing great by the IP they have; and thus turning off potential partners. What is a VtM via D&amp;D 5e book going to actually do to convince people that Paradox knows what it's doing with the WoD, and is going to be a good working partner for other projects? It isn't going to sell $150 million worth of profits. Nobody but WotC does that with a TT RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T16:51:51-08:00","id":1502895,"title":"","content":"First rule of changing something is you have to start somewhere and actually try to do something differently than you have before.<br /> <br /> The point of trying a VtM5e isn\u2019t to get $150 million in sales\u2026 its to get more eyeballs on the VtM IP than there are presently by reaching out to a consumer base that, overall, won\u2019t even look at an IP that isn\u2019t compatible with 5e.<br /> <br /> Its a consumer group estimated at around 13.7 MILLION currently active players. Why would you NOT be interested in trying to sell to that market given how adjacent it is to the product you already make? Who cares if you only reach one percent of them, that still 137,000 sets of eyeballs looking at VtM who probably don\u2019t even know it exists currently.<br /> <br /> How many currently active players does the WoD combined have?<br /> <br /> The suggestion is because one of the easiest ways to start somewhere is with the low-hanging fruit of an industry that is already familiar and uses all the production and distribution methods you already have in place and has a massive number of prospects you could try to reach.<br /> <br /> You produce something for people outside the existing fans to talk about and maybe have a few industry articles written about. It\u2019s a starting point to get more people aware so when your next KS launches you have more eyeballs than there are now looking for the words \u201cVampire the Masquerade.\u201d<br /> <br /> Is that all that should be done? No. But it\u2019s a step.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T02:55:29-08:00","id":1502919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502895#post1502895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First rule of changing something is you have to start somewhere and actually try to do something differently than you have before.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK... so they should handle their video game development process differently because their current model is producing shit results.<br /> <br /> VtM: Bloodlines was pretty much the only enduring pop-culture/mainstream product in the entire catalogue. And being a video game it had huge reach despite falling into being a cult classic. Over the last ~20 years BL 1 has consistently been in most video game website's lists of best cult games, most underappreciated games, games everyone should play at least once, etc.<br /> <br /> The first trailer for BL 2 rode that have over 1.5 million views on YouTube. Paradox's main YouTube account has over 350K subscribers. LA By Night had really good viewership for a non-D&amp;D actual play stream and for having to switch platforms... it even had guest spots from Critical Role cast members.<br /> <br /> Making a d20 book for the game to maybe get 1/4 million eyeballs on their products is pointless because they've gotten way more than that multiple times.<br /> <br /> The problem now is that those eyeballs don't like where things are headed. BL 2 is in development hell. Other games are getting eyeballs for the wrong reason. LA by Night ended and NY by Night doesn't seem to be hitting quite as high, etc.<br /> <br /> Anyone that's going to give a VtM with D&amp;D 5e rules game a look has most likely already seen major parts of this. Every major gaming news site has covered portions of it just like they keep listing BL 1 as a cult classic people should get whenever it goes up on sale on Steam or GOG.<br /> <br /> Paradox's problem is not getting eyeballs on their products. It's putting out products people want to stay invested in (either side of that statement has had problems).<br /> <br /> Paradox <b>is a video game company</b>. The change they need to make is whatever change results in a good VtM video game. Making a VtM TT RPG book with a different rule set doesn't lead to a good video game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its a consumer group estimated at around 13.7 MILLION currently active players. Why would you NOT be interested in trying to sell to that market given how adjacent it is to the product you already make? Who cares if you only reach one percent of them, that still 137,000 sets of eyeballs looking at VtM who probably don\u2019t even know it exists currently. </div> </div> </div>There's a much bigger audience out there to tap into that already knows VtM exists already is why.<br /> <br /> The fact that the vast majority of products that are compatible with D&amp;D 5e will never sell 50K copies is why.<br /> <br /> The fact that bad games hurt brand value (see: VtM: Swansong) despite any initial hype is why. Though this isn't to say you can't make a good VtM-like game in d20, but that's a lot of work to capture what people remember about VtM (which is mostly, again, BL 1's experience) in a positive way that engages fans; not just slapping something together in a year and shoving it out the door with &quot;5e Compatible&quot; on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The suggestion is because one of the easiest ways to start somewhere is with the low-hanging fruit of an industry that is already familiar and uses all the production and distribution methods you already have in place and has a massive number of prospects you could try to reach. </div> </div> </div>There's no substantiation to this claim. &quot;D&amp;D compatible&quot; is not some massive sales driver for pretty much anyone other than WotC. It doesn't even actually make that much for them either, as the vast majority of their profits are the PHB and DMG.<br /> <br /> The suggestion makes no sense because it's based on the most superficial reading of the industry. You continue to skip any points made that try to point out all the stuff you're just assuming away because &quot;D&amp;D 5e compatible&quot;is apparently magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T08:01:19-08:00","id":1502931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502919#post1502919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a d20 book for the game to maybe get 1/4 million eyeballs on their products is pointless because they've gotten way more than that multiple times.<br /> <br /> There's no substantiation to this claim. &quot;D&amp;D compatible&quot; is not some massive sales driver for pretty much anyone other than WotC. It doesn't even actually make that much for them either, as the vast majority of their profits are the PHB and DMG.<br /> <br /> The suggestion makes no sense because it's based on the most superficial reading of the industry. You continue to skip any points made that try to point out all the stuff you're just assuming away because &quot;D&amp;D 5e compatible&quot;is apparently magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>To support this even further. Kobold Press Tome of Beasts is one of the most popular and reprinted third party 5e supplements, designed and written by a group of well known people with ties to WotC and their original 5E adventures. On DTRPG it's considered a mere mithral seller, and most of the OP &amp; nuWW books are considered Adamantine sellers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T11:23:19-08:00","id":1502942,"title":"","content":"It's make sense that they would changes things about a setting when it gets adapted into another medium to drum up further interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T15:13:28-08:00","id":1502962,"title":"","content":"I don't think most setting changes are about drumming up interest. The biggest driver in setting changes when adapting a work is to compensate for the adaptation process. There's things that work in one medium that just don't work in others.<br /> <br /> A simple example from the new The Last of US TV show: they changed how the infection spreads. In the video games, the infection is capable of airborne spread via spores, so in the video games there's a lot of time spent wearing gas masks. The video games are also predominantly 3rd person over the shoulder camera angles, so you don't really see your character in a mask all the time. That's a lot harder on a TV show. Everyone in gas masks means it's harder to tell characters apart, it's harder for actors to emote, it's harder to visually indicate dangerous levels of spores in the air without a video game's HUD. In this specific case they didn't want constant comparisons to The Mandalorian with Pedro Pascal playing a constantly masked character escorting a special child around.<br /> <br /> Obviously in the end, the goal is to get lots of people to watch it, but by making it good as a TV show, not just change to change from the games to be different.<br /> <br /> There are also other reasons to change things when adaptations happen. Multiple Naughty Dog people that worked on The Last of Us games and are working on the new show have expressed how often the TV writers just come up with stuff that's better than the game's version was. Things that if they could go back in time and redo the original games, the show's story beats would be what was always the case sort of stuff. Adaptations are a chance to do those sorts of changes that you basically can't in most mediums (and even if you pull a George Lucas and redo your old movies with changes, it tends to piss people off way more than continuity errors that come from adapting into different mediums).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T15:36:31-08:00","id":1502963,"title":"","content":"Personally I've always got the Impression Paradox probably wernt really paying attention to what the origional design team of v5 were doing and if it synergised with their long terms aims. The whole attitude v5 has to combat smacks of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T17:15:47-08:00","id":1502971,"title":"","content":"On the subject of possibly using different TTRPG engines/licenses, it's been mentioned before that the sort of success Paradox was hoping to have was numbers akin to the Avatar Legends Kickstarter, numbers that rattled the cage and got a whole lot of people realizing that there were alternatives to the d20 license. In that respect, as well as how the Powered by The Apocalypse's tight focus on narrative-driven games is a good fit for World of Darkness own &quot;RPG's-as-art&quot; mantra and would do a good job bringing the games overall into the ways games are played now instead of relying on the 80's/90's models, a launch of a PbtA version of World products that managed to communicate in the branding it's mechanical similarities to Avatar Legends is just as viable a option for resolving the issue as releasing a d20 version of World, if not even <i>better</i> because one of World's selling points is that it is gaming for an audience that doesn't like Dungeons and Dragons, either for it's system, it's narrative idiom, or both.<br /> <br /> The thing of the matter on that, though, is you can hear how hollow and little that actually matters. It's changing the mechanical idiom and structure of the game for the purpose of what's fundamentally a surface level result, like arguing that the reason Cyberpunk 2077 was disappointing on release because it was released for Xbox, Playstation, and PC, and if someone had made it for the Nintendo Switch, it would have been uproariously approved of-not only does it evaluate what amounts to a wrapping paper consideration on the same level as deep and fundamental problems, but it's execution would probably make it an actively worse game.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Paradox's take on World is that it's basiclaly just a bad product all around (with all apologies to fans who do enjoy what's been made), a result of a failure of oversight on a myopic development that has devolved into a desperate attempt to right the ship that's...not working too well, and the only thing that's gonna fix that is taking the time to make a thoroughly good, as-unimpeachable-as-possible product as possible that will get a lot of eyes on it, and that's a problem when you have returns to make.<br /> <br /> If I were to make suggestions on what they can actually do that's close to this vein, it would probably be to first cut away all multimedia plans and focus on just one medium-and if I can be wildly salacious here, I would encourage Paradox to stop thinking about is <i>as</i> tabletop games instead focus purely on the franchise as a video game property, as it's not only what they're good ostensibly good at already and video games are a pretty wide market that will still overlap and interest existing fans, but it also lets them soft reboot and explore different overarching idiom and structures and find a take on the material that fixes their problems and maybe better allows for forward development-and just focus on making one (maybe a few) products <i>really really well</i>. If I were to get a little more wild in suggestion, I might suggest pulling a Marvel Gambit, where instead of trying to fix the mess they made out of their bigger name properties in the franchise, they pick one of the b-or-c listers and focus on making that as good as possible-I know it's technically not World of Darkness, but I'd personally pitch Orpheus (and if we stick to the idea of it being video games, I would also strongly encourage a resistance to temptation to make a game that shares a lot of the trends common today-resist the open world, the crafting, etc. etc. in the interest of making it stand out as much as possible).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T17:42:52-08:00","id":1502974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502971#post1502971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were to make suggestions on what they can actually do that's close to this vein, it would probably be to first cut away all multimedia plans and focus on just one medium-and if I can be wildly salacious here, I would encourage Paradox to stop thinking about is <i>as</i> tabletop games instead focus purely on the franchise as a video game property, as it's not only what they're good ostensibly good at already and video games are a pretty wide market that will still overlap and interest existing fans, but it also lets them soft reboot and explore different overarching idiom and structures and find a take on the material that fixes their problems and maybe better allows for forward development-and just focus on making one (maybe a few) products <i>really really well</i>. If I were to get a little more wild in suggestion, I might suggest pulling a Marvel Gambit, where instead of trying to fix the mess they made out of their bigger name properties in the franchise, they pick one of the b-or-c listers and focus on making that as good as possible-I know it's technically not World of Darkness, but I'd personally pitch Orpheus (and if we stick to the idea of it being video games, I would also strongly encourage a resistance to temptation to make a game that shares a lot of the trends common today-resist the open world, the crafting, etc. etc. in the interest of making it stand out as much as possible).</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read about Orpheus on the wiki, (which is admittedly, very little), it seems like a vey interesing and fun gameline, and I dont understand why it isnt more popular among the fanbase. The powers of the Shades is also very intriguing and seems like it would be right up the alley of many fans who enjoy the WOD. It would be amazing if paradox could create a game that is true to what Orpheus is, perhaps instead of focusing on the graphics they could focus on making a great game, similar to how indie games are made. Perhaps it can even be used to help people discover the other gamelines inherent to both the WOD and COD.<br /> <br /> Hopefully paradox goes down this path instead of the one they have been currently taking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T18:18:34-08:00","id":1502978,"title":"","content":"Orpheus's biggest problem was just how close to the end of the cWoD era it wa released for. It's hard to say how big the impact was, but it had almost no time to build up a place within the fandom before the cWoD ended and CofD 1e began.<br /> <br /> Having played through the core story, there are a few strange quirks that cause the PCs' &quot;level&quot; to not quite line up with what happens in the story. For example picking Backgrounds without spoiling yourself on what happens, and just going with what makes sense, can feel very off. Orpheus PCs have one of the weakest starting points in the cWoD but the game doesn't seem to realize they did that and thinks they start with more stuff than they really do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T18:23:05-08:00","id":1502979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502978#post1502978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orpheus's biggest problem was just how close to the end of the cWoD era it wa released for. It's hard to say how big the impact was, but it had almost no time to build up a place within the fandom before the cWoD ended and CofD 1e began.<br /> <br /> Having played through the core story, there are a few strange quirks that cause the PCs' &quot;level&quot; to not quite line up with what happens in the story. For example picking Backgrounds without spoiling yourself on what happens, and just going with what makes sense, can feel very off. Orpheus PCs have one of the weakest starting points in the cWoD but the game doesn't seem to realize they did that and thinks they start with more stuff than they really do.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of the Marvel Gambit, something like Dreaming or Oblivion is probably a better swing, admittedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T20:14:43-08:00","id":1502993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502978#post1502978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orpheus's biggest problem was just how close to the end of the cWoD era it wa released for. It's hard to say how big the impact was, but it had almost no time to build up a place within the fandom before the cWoD ended and CofD 1e began.<br /> <br /> Having played through the core story, there are a few strange quirks that cause the PCs' &quot;level&quot; to not quite line up with what happens in the story. For example picking Backgrounds without spoiling yourself on what happens, and just going with what makes sense, can feel very off. Orpheus PCs have one of the weakest starting points in the cWoD but the game doesn't seem to realize they did that and thinks they start with more stuff than they really do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, I wasnt aware charachters from orpheus were that much weaker. But i guess that why not many talk about the game line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T00:24:02-08:00","id":1503003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502979#post1502979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of the Marvel Gambit, something like Dreaming or Oblivion is probably a better swing, admittedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Orpheus still has a lot of pros for that particular approach. A big one being that Orpheus agents start as normal people that get recruited into a company with a reputation for weird things. The (still human) PCs aren't really expected to know much about what's really going on. There's a lot to be said of using one of the few games where a starting level PC is probably going to know less about the WoD than the player does. My comment to Hello was really just a direct answer to why it didn't really take off that well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1502993#post1502993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see, I wasnt aware charachters from orpheus were that much weaker. But i guess that why not many talk about the game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it is a comparative thing, not an objective thing. On their own, and with the right story to play them in, there's nothing wrong with their stating package. It's just quickly apparent when you're more familiar with the other games in the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T10:38:11-08:00","id":1503044,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1502962]I don't think most setting changes are about drumming up interest. The biggest driver in setting changes when adapting a work is to compensate for the adaptation process. There's things that work in one medium that just don't work in others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Isn't drumming up interest what it's all about to get more people interested in a setting or at least a major driving factor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T11:51:29-08:00","id":1503048,"title":"","content":"That's why marketing is a whole profession yes. One of the reasons people can make whole careers around marketing is because there isn't some simple formula to drumming up interest.<br /> <br /> While there are common wisdom &quot;rules&quot; in marketing (for example, you always want to put a positive spin on thing like, &quot;we made it better,&quot; instead of, &quot;we fixed what was wrong,&quot; even if it's the exactly same change being made), the complexities of industry are a lot to navigate. A big thing here, is that conversion rates are going to matter. That is, how many people get interested in something compared to how many people engage further later in time. It's really not hard to make a video that will go viral on the Internet and get millions of views. It is much, much harder to know how to make a video that will also result in people say, buying your product. <br /> <br /> Changing things just to change them is not considered a good tactic for converting attention to sales. Existing fans (those people that are going to care the most about changes anyway) are going to want changes for reasons they can understand. New/potential fans are easily confused and thus put off by being told about changes as hype if they don't know why that change is supposed to be good.<br /> <br /> So, back to my examples: The marketing for The Last of US is not, &quot;we changed it because we just thought it you'd all rather see this part set in Kansas City instead of Pittsburgh,&quot; but rather, &quot;we changed how Henry and Sam were introduced to make sure these pivotal and iconic characters impact TV audiences like they did fans of the games.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, the reason they changed from Pittsburgh to Kansas city is really a mixture of scheduling and securing shooting locations, and a desire to have the main characters move at a bit faster clip than the games because you don't want to make the climax feel rushed so they moved a major plot point farther along the physical path to make it feel like the characters were moving across the country in line with the show's pacing. But none of that drums up attention. The change was going to creating feedback because that's the nature of adaptations,so the marketing team has the job of heading off negative feedback by highlighting the strengths of any changes rather than dwelling on just the fact that things changed, or the minutiae of practical behind-the-scenes issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T00:28:48-08:00","id":1503115,"title":"","content":"People want more of the same, not original ideas. Everyone complains about how hollywood makes sequels and reboots rather than original ideas, but that's because people buy into sequels and reboots rather than original ideas, and sometimes they get unreasonably angry when something near and dear to them gets changed too much. In the case of VTM, it<i> mostly</i> worked very well before, and all the changes seem like stupid stunts/change for change sake/ that weird urge writers get where they're supposed to copy something but their ego/lack of love for the source material makes them want to reimagine it as something completely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T02:44:10-08:00","id":1503121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503115#post1503115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People want more of the same, not original ideas. Everyone complains about how hollywood makes sequels and reboots rather than original ideas, but that's because people buy into sequels and reboots rather than original ideas, and sometimes they get unreasonably angry when something near and dear to them gets changed too much. In the case of VTM, it<i> mostly</i> worked very well before, and all the changes seem like stupid stunts/change for change sake/ that weird urge writers get where they're supposed to copy something but their ego/lack of love for the source material makes them want to reimagine it as something completely different.</div> </div> </div> </div>People don't want more of the same. It's just easier to sell them on what they're familiar with. And in an environment where creativity is constrained by how profitable it has to be, of course it ends up like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T03:13:16-08:00","id":1503125,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure we've debated this before, but....<br /> <br /> That's equally off the mark as the idea that people change things in adaptations just to excite potential audiences.<br /> <br /> Humans are simply not that easy to sum up. If you even wanted to give it an honest shot, it would be something like this: humans like variations on a theme.<br /> <br /> We like a familiar core theme because those core themes resonate strongly with previous experiences, but we desire art that adds unique and experimental ideas to that core theme, because hewing too close to a core theme turns it repetitive and dull. It's fairly simple to argue that the true skill of an artist is finding the lines between too close and too far for a core theme and playing withing that amorphous space with creativity and fresh ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T04:34:33-08:00","id":1503129,"title":"","content":"I was exaggerating a bit for effect. Few people went into <i>The Force Awakens</i> and were ecstatic to get a prettier but worse <i>A New Hope</i>. But that said, despite the terrible downward trend, people still showed up for <i>RoS</i>, because it's still <i>Star Wars</i> and a mythology they're familiar with and they'll watch it even knowing it's going to be crap. Even as a franchise shows it's limits for how bad it can get and still have people watching, there are still people who will watch something familiar despite knowing they won't enjoy it.<br /> <br /> More direct to your idea that people just want variations of a theme: A lot of people were extremely hostile to the <i>RoboCop</i> reboot... which was a fairly passable movie. It hit most of the same beats and themes of the original film. The actor performances were better... It just wasn't as fun. (but like, ED-209 being incredibly clumsy probably wouldn't work so well with modern expectations of how killer robots would work, so I can't really blame them too much for being more serious)<br /> <br /> <br /> VTM offers a great smorgasbord of potential themes and a lot of ideas for stories. Unfortunately V5 stripped most of them away to focus on an artificially narrow vision of the product. IE Fledgling anarchs engaging in &quot;street level&quot; play and wallowing in their own misery.<br /> <br /> People often fly into a rage when new themes and ideas deny something in previous stories. Going back to an unfortunately popular example, <i>SW</i>:<i>TLJ</i> openly refutes a lot of ideas people had about <i>Star Wars</i> and there's now like a hundred thousand hour+ videos on why that's a problem on youtube and I'm amazed by the view counts (I think it's just a bad film from a non-star wars fan perspective, but even as a fan of film critique I'm not wading into that). Meanwhile Andor is tonally and thematically completely different to other Star Wars products and everyone who got past the first few boring episodes considers it a masterpiece; VTM likewise had excellent room for stories, and you could run your chronicle like <i>A New Hope</i> or like <i>Andor</i> and it would still fit. But come V5 you really don't have so many options. V20 gave us every option, V5 gives us like... a few. That makes it less enduring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-15-2023, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T12:42:24-08:00","id":1503157,"title":"","content":"MWIS, dude, you know bringing up Star Wars like this is just going to get the mods annoyed. Why even go there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503129#post1503129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More direct to your idea that people just want variations of a theme: A lot of people were extremely hostile to the <i>RoboCop</i> reboot... which was a fairly passable movie. It hit most of the same beats and themes of the original film. The actor performances were better... <b>It just wasn't as fun.</b> (but like, ED-209 being incredibly clumsy probably wouldn't work so well with modern expectations of how killer robots would work, so I can't really blame them too much for being more serious)</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolding mine.<br /> <br /> That's the problem. The reboot's creators might have been a fairly good (though most critics don't agree it was all that good) movie that didn't work as a Robocop movie because it strayed too far from the core themes. Instead of trying play in that liminal space I pointed early, they flipped around a hugely important part of the original story. In the original, Robocop finds out that he was once human, and struggles to find his humanity (and perhaps soul) that's still hidden under the layers of code used to animate his corpse. In the remake they made it so he thought he was human with some replacement parts, only to find out over the story how much they were overriding his free will underneath that.<br /> <br /> Those are two very different core themes to tackle. The original movie is a variation on Frankenstein: the doctor is the real monster, not his confused and erratic creation who, in the end, is the one that truly embraces what it is to be human despite everything that happened. Or in terms more fitting for this forum the original Robocop is a Promethean story, and the remake is a Vampire story (where a human is changed into something else and struggles to maintain their humanity in light how just how different they really are).<br /> <br /> If you want to a movie being told you were seeing a new Frankenstein movie and got a new Dracula movie, it could be a great Dracula movie, but it's still going to annoying most people.<br /> <br /> There's also a huge tonal differences in the films. The original is much more farcical and exaggerated in its satire. Many people accredit that balancing act to why the movie has had such an enduring appeal despite major cultural shifts (including views of police militarization). Even by the standards of when the original came out, it was oddly campy and comedic in unexpected ways (to long term audience approval). The mixing of dark drama and over the top moments went together well to highlight the targets of the satire involved and in many ways help them stay relevant towards changing cultural contexts. <br /> <br /> The reboot is a much more straight drama and the satire feels more forced for it. If you even want to consider it satirical because at a point it's just making value judgements via story rather than really trying to encourage subversive critical thought. By missing so many of the comedic beats (esp. because of the change in character development noted already) it lost of a lot of why people wanted out of a Robocop film.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> VTM offers a great smorgasbord of potential themes and a lot of ideas for stories. Unfortunately V5 stripped most of them away to focus on an artificially narrow vision of the product. IE Fledgling anarchs engaging in &quot;street level&quot; play and wallowing in their own misery. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure most of us agree on this part of things. The conversation has, for a bit now, been talking about how VtM could escape this, not if it's true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People often fly into a rage when new themes and ideas deny something in previous stories. </div> </div> </div>There is, however, a big difference between removing things that were explicitly in previous works, compared to establishing something in contrast to fan speculations.<br /> <br /> V5 objectively makes things that used to be possible in the rules no longer possible via mechanical changes. You can't master both necromancy and shadow manipulation... because instead of those being two different powers, those are one power now and you have to pick which side to focus on if you want to master one. My old DA Lasombra that decided to opt out of Lasombra political nonsense and join the Road of Bones - including studying Necroomancy from Road followers more naturally talented in those arts - can't work in V5 without house rules.<br /> <br /> The idea of an era of a Second Inquisition is a separate matter. The idea that around 2010 secular governments starting taking the existence of vampires as a more serious threat is a big change, and it might cut off some old stories if you suddenly insert that into a preexisting game, but the concept doesn't &quot;deny&quot; what was. It actually plays a lot into what was setup already. How one feels about V5's execution of the topic is a where people really tend to disagree. I really don't like how the V5 setting established a more unified global initiative for a number of reasons, but I can't deny that a big one is that it completely violates my personal feelings about how many of those groups should operate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T13:27:07-08:00","id":1503161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503115#post1503115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People want more of the same, not original ideas. Everyone complains about how hollywood makes sequels and reboots rather than original ideas, but that's because people buy into sequels and reboots rather than original ideas, and sometimes they get unreasonably angry when something near and dear to them gets changed too much. In the case of VTM, it<i> mostly</i> worked very well before, and all the changes seem like stupid stunts/change for change sake/ that weird urge writers get where they're supposed to copy something but their ego/lack of love for the source material makes them want to reimagine it as something completely different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I do want clarity on something here: When you say <i>people</i> want more of the same, are you <i>also</i> saying <i>you</i> want more of the same?<br /> <br /> THe rest of your argument is hard for me to grok, because this hasn't proven true in my experience, so I'm trying to understand the perspective at work here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T23:16:45-08:00","id":1503205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503161#post1503161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I do want clarity on something here: When you say <i>people</i> want more of the same, are you <i>also</i> saying <i>you</i> want more of the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to admit it, but yes.<br /> For movies I have this massive to-watch list of recommended films that keeps piling up, but the movies I watch and actually enjoy have some strong biases to them. To say nothing of computer games where despite having a massive library built up over 15 years I've really only properly played half of them because learning new stuff or getting invested in a new story is intimidating. As much as I'd like to consider myself open minded, and I am certainly a person who can change his mind, it's very easy to fall into patterns and natural to have strong preferences.<br /> <br /> Also like, there are bands out there that make all their music sound the same for a reason. Over 45 years of albums AC/DC maintains the same sound, and they know it, it's a strength to them. I'm baffled by a few friends liking Sabbaton because that's even more extreme as they've clearly just got like, one really long song. On the other extreme you've got Gorillaz, where every song is very different and it's disorienting and off-putting and weird and I'm half convinced you have to lie to yourself to say you like it all. Now yeah, you can argue about this being a matter of building a strong i Identity, but AC/DC fans have never been disappointed, while Tool fans will always be comparing New Tool to Old Tool and Gorillaz fans will be trying to cherrypick because they should know it's hopeless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> V20 was in a pretty nice spot, imperfect, but a pretty good place to be in. V5 feels like a stunt with the amount changed. <b>It's probably worth noting that when you have a game about ancient, scarcely changing monsters, it seems pretty incongruent to have such a wildly changing metaplot outside of a Gehenna scenario</b>. I suppose V5 is a Gehenna scenario, and it's a little weird to kill the franchise like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-16-2023, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T00:05:14-08:00","id":1503208,"title":"","content":"Or maybe people just like stuff you don't?<br /> <br /> As for cherry-picking, you just said AC/DC fans have never been disappointed or have had Old AC/DC vs. New AC/DC comparisons? This might be an age thing, but the loss of Bon Scott and his replacement by Brian Johnson was hugely divisive. That was just 43 years ago (quite nearly literally, Bon Scott died Feb. 19th 1980), so saying 45 years of albums for a band that's been around for 50 and therefore just skipping over the Bon Scott years and the change in lead singer definitely feels like some picking of cherries.. I've heard more than a feel people say that with Malcolm Young's passing, that AC/DC should call it quits for good and end on the high-ish point that was PWR/UP instead of trying to keep going (esp. with the average age of the band members making it increasingly obvious that their style of music and performance is getting to be more and more of a struggle to do).<br /> <br /> While certainly in small niche circles people will never stop fighting over David Lee Roth's Van Halen vs. Sammy Hagar's Van Halen, something I've noticed over time is that those things are more moments in time than real trends. Some bands endure because they appeal to fans of a very specific style of music, and other bands endure because they're eclectic and people like that you can throw on <i>A Hard Day's Night</i> for one mood, or <i>Sgt.Pepper's</i> for a different mood (and seriously consider how iconic the Beatles are for a band that only lasted 10 years, and how diverse their music was).<br /> <br /> So yeah, there are bands out there that stick to a very specific style... but plenty don't. There's no objective right or wrong to it. There's just what artists can and will enjoy doing, and what fans will like. Being willing to change things up every album is as much of a brand identity as having one specific sound a band really focuses on.<br /> <br /> You don't need to ascribe negative motivations to Gorillaz fans because they like how diverse the styles are and their albums can be more like listening to a very well curated streaming playlist instead of one band's specific choices about trying to make a coherent album in tone. Lots of people listen to the radio, or stream random playlists within preset parameters, without them lying about liking that experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T00:37:57-08:00","id":1503209,"title":"","content":"A quick case in point, because the dragon got poked anyways: I like The Last Jedi, and I explicitly like it because while it was the latest Star Wars movie (and even after it wasn't) I was fucking bored of Star Wars and the general threads and trends that series was committed to that contributed to basically everything becoming a soup of sameyness, and The Last Jedi flipped so many of those things on their head. To hone in on one thing that really did it for me, if you had told me before Last Jedi that Rey was a Palpatine, I might've run with it wel enough-but after just how damn refreshing it was for Rey to be a nobody of no importance who <i>desperately</i> wanted to be special that Last Jedi made her, her turning out to be a Palpatine is the reason I won't watch Rise of Skywalker, because the idea of Star Wars being a story of Skywalkers and Palpatines is one of those thigns that was so damn repetitive that made Star Wars boring in the first place.<br /> <br /> I also hope that the question of &quot;When I assume something of most people, am I part of what I mean by most people?&quot; is a useful question for the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T00:53:17-08:00","id":1503212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503209#post1503209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Last Jedi flipped so many of those things on their head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did it though? The setting is effectively were it was 40 years ago by the end of movie. Plucky underdogs vs big empire led by evil wizard. I've never really been into star wars but nothing about it really challenged me or made me re consider anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-16-2023, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T00:59:49-08:00","id":1503213,"title":"","content":"You're overly getting into details here and I think it's weird that you've somehow come to the conclusion that other people liking things I don't is a problem for me. That feels a little personal. I was just suggesting that a lot of people like to find a lane and don't veer much outside that lane.<br /> <br /> I like Gorillaz. But they've released some real stinkers in trying to be experimental. A fan doesn't need to like every song. It's normal to cherry pick (especially if we're going through old bands. At one point I thought <i>Black Sabbath</i> could've done no wrong, because my Dad and playlist algorithms had carefully curated an excellent selection. They certainly have stinkers)<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, this is way off topic.<br /> Vampire the masquerade is an excellent sandbox. It's the real world but more shit and with magic that hides itself. Thematically you've got near infinite possibilities: Gothic or Romantic, gritty and political, action extravaganza, farcical comedy... they all work. Is your horror based on your declining humanity from your disease or in the political realities you find yourself in, or is it simply you're a little monster in a world with bigger monsters. No matter what your preference, Vampire can accommodate you. If you like Opera, you're good. Gregorian chant? You're good. Folk? Good. If you like punk, you're good, if you like post punk, you're good, and if you like Jazz... I'm sure there's a place for you, somewhere. From a writer's point of view, this is the best. <br /> <br /> V5 is a much more limited sandbox. You either dance to the tune the mechanics and setting puts you in or you play another edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-16-2023, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T01:27:18-08:00","id":1503215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503213#post1503213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, this is way off topic.<br /> Vampire the masquerade is an excellent sandbox. It's the real world but more shit and with magic that hides itself. Thematically you've got near infinite possibilities: Gothic or Romantic, gritty and political, action extravaganza, farcical comedy... they all work. Is your horror based on your declining humanity from your disease or in the political realities you find yourself in, or is it simply you're a little monster in a world with bigger monsters. No matter what your preference, Vampire can accommodate you. If you like Opera, you're good. Gregorian chant? You're good. Folk? Good. If you like punk, you're good, if you like post punk, you're good, and if you like Jazz... I'm sure there's a place for you, somewhere. From a writer's point of view, this is the best.<br /> <br /> V5 is a much more limited sandbox. You either dance to the tune the mechanics and setting puts you in or you play another edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of the things I clocked early on is how well wod does black comedy. The amount of ic snark and situational humour that you can get in is quite remarkable. I recall something as simple as having the lasombra (and getting pissed when they realise why) in the back middle seat of a car or snickering about clan eccentricities is very fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-16-2023, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T03:27:05-08:00","id":1503219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503213#post1503213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're overly getting into details here and I think it's weird that you've somehow come to the conclusion that other people liking things I don't is a problem for me. That feels a little personal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brushing of the major change to AC/DC's sound and style that came with Bon Scott's death and Brian Johnson replacing him isn't really a small detail what you're claiming their sound has never changed. That's more of a &quot;direct point counter to your claim&quot; sort of thing. If you want to say, &quot;sure, AC/DC wasn't a great example because it's been so long since that I wasn't really thinking about it,&quot; great. But that's not me getting caught up in details.<br /> <br /> I've come to that conclusion because you <b>consistently</b> take a position that things you don't like being popular is somehow an objective wrong that must be shut down with every word you type. How am I not supposed to come to this conclusion based on our discussion history? When have you actually just been chill with some people liking stuff that you don't like, when you could rail on how your opinion about something must be objectively true? Seriously. Link me. I would love to be wrong about this.<br /> <br /> And because of that you make everything personal. You don't just say, &quot;I like some Gorillaz tracks, but how much they change up styles and tones is off-putting to me,&quot; you say, &quot;I'm half convinced people that say the like this are lying to themselves.&quot; Why wouldn't anyone that's a fan of the band not find that &quot;a little personal&quot; and feel clapping back a bit for it? You consistently make very broad statements about what people are &quot;really&quot; like, and you don't think you're making things a little personal by doing that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was just suggesting that a lot of people like to find a lane and don't veer much outside that lane. </div> </div> </div>Then... why not just say that? You never said that in the last two pages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like Gorillaz </div> </div> </div>Interesting to say that now instead of before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But they've released some real stinkers in trying to be experimental. </div> </div> </div>And? Who said they didn't? What does the fact that nobody (and especially not artists) is perfect and always puts out 100% perfect stuff have to do with anything anyone was saying?<br /> <br /> How is this not just a goal-post shift?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yeah, this is way off topic. </div> </div> </div>So it rehashing why you like pre-V5 VtM over V5.<br /> <br /> Pre-V5 VtM, for all the thing we both agree on why we like it more, managed to fall off the mainstream radar well before V5 came into the picture. While it was never intended to do so, V20 didn't send it back into it's early 00s status. Negative perceptions around the franchise existing before Paradox bought it after the WoD MMO got canned, just like BL 2 going into indefinite development is hurting the prospects of mainstream rival is doing now.<br /> <br /> Even if I really don't like where V5 went in terms of narrowing play options, and H5 and W5 are headed in even worse directions for me in that regard, that's not an inherently bad call for mainstream prospects for the IP. D&amp;D's enduring popularity is a very narrow and very addictive game play loop: action-adventure quest for XP and loot, use XP and loot to get stronger, go on harder action-adventure quests for better XP and loot rewards, repeat. For all the creative groups can do way more with the rules than that, that's what the rules are all about. That's essentially been the rules since the beginning (except for when XP and loot were the same thing). D&amp;D's mechanically narrowness is undeniably successful no matter how much some of us prefer games that are much broader in what the rules enable and encourage. <br /> <br /> If your goal is to make VtM more accessible (and thus more likely to be adapted to other forms of entertainment), narrowing it's base/default scope is a completely valid approach to take. You still have to do it well, and then manage it well, but if done right there's no reason to expect it wouldn't work to make the brand easier to get back to the mainstream.<br /> <br /> From a non-interaction fiction writer's point of view the &quot;anything can find a home in here,&quot; kitchen sink is not best. How is a novel writer, or TV script doctor supposed to know how to make their story more VtM-esque if there is no core VtM loop people are 100% expecting. D&amp;D's narrower play-loop is much, much easier to write in if your goal is to keep some level of brand consistency. Without it you're way more likely to get style over substance, and lose the edge you need to get back to mainstream status. <br /> <br /> Even for interactive fiction it causes problems. There's whole sets of memes about how nobody actually finishes Elder Scrolls games. You have this gigantic sandbox, and the main questline is the easiest thing on Earth to completely forget about, and dozens of hours later, you feel like you've played enough of the game to last you for ages... and you never got past the mandatory intro main quest missions. If that kind of broadness was good for video-game writing, you'd wouldn't see that tendency to get so wrapped up in side-quests and exploration that you never play the main game that is so often lamented about super-sandboxy game design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","