,"edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T05:18:31-08:00","id":1503226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503225#post1503225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just one small point: now with most groups using milestone leveling, XP isn\u2019t really a thing anymore. Plus the modern rules in 5e are much friendlier to rp than they used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feeding and elysium combat are pretty bloated are very gamey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T11:18:27-08:00","id":1503250,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Amethyst was talking about D&amp;D 5e's rules, not V5, when discussion how it's an improvement over how RP is integrated into the system. Esp. with the talk of milestone leveling instead of encounter XP bean counting.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with the aside being made, though I don't think it really changes the core D&amp;D play-loop in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T10:32:24-08:00","id":1503386,"title":"","content":"Like it's been said before. There is no original ideas but creative takes on old ones or words to that effect and I'm down for a different take on an old story as long it's true to the spirit of the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T18:35:39-08:00","id":1503973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1503219#post1503219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brushing of the major change to AC/DC's sound and style that came with Bon Scott's death and Brian Johnson replacing him isn't really a small detail what you're claiming their sound has never changed. That's more of a &quot;direct point counter to your claim&quot; sort of thing. If you want to say, &quot;sure, AC/DC wasn't a great example because it's been so long since that I wasn't really thinking about it,&quot; great. But that's not me getting caught up in details.<br /> <br /> I've come to that conclusion because you <b>consistently</b> take a position that things you don't like being popular is somehow an objective wrong that must be shut down with every word you type. How am I not supposed to come to this conclusion based on our discussion history? When have you actually just been chill with some people liking stuff that you don't like, when you could rail on how your opinion about something must be objectively true? Seriously. Link me. I would love to be wrong about this.<br /> <br /> And because of that you make everything personal. You don't just say, &quot;I like some Gorillaz tracks, but how much they change up styles and tones is off-putting to me,&quot; you say, &quot;I'm half convinced people that say the like this are lying to themselves.&quot; Why wouldn't anyone that's a fan of the band not find that &quot;a little personal&quot; and feel clapping back a bit for it? You consistently make very broad statements about what people are &quot;really&quot; like, and you don't think you're making things a little personal by doing that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then... why not just say that? You never said that in the last two pages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Interesting to say that now instead of before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And? Who said they didn't? What does the fact that nobody (and especially not artists) is perfect and always puts out 100% perfect stuff have to do with anything anyone was saying?<br /> <br /> How is this not just a goal-post shift?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So it rehashing why you like pre-V5 VtM over V5.<br /> <br /> Pre-V5 VtM, for all the thing we both agree on why we like it more, managed to fall off the mainstream radar well before V5 came into the picture. While it was never intended to do so, V20 didn't send it back into it's early 00s status. Negative perceptions around the franchise existing before Paradox bought it after the WoD MMO got canned, just like BL 2 going into indefinite development is hurting the prospects of mainstream rival is doing now.<br /> <br /> Even if I really don't like where V5 went in terms of narrowing play options, and H5 and W5 are headed in even worse directions for me in that regard, that's not an inherently bad call for mainstream prospects for the IP. D&amp;D's enduring popularity is a very narrow and very addictive game play loop: action-adventure quest for XP and loot, use XP and loot to get stronger, go on harder action-adventure quests for better XP and loot rewards, repeat. For all the creative groups can do way more with the rules than that, that's what the rules are all about. That's essentially been the rules since the beginning (except for when XP and loot were the same thing). D&amp;D's mechanically narrowness is undeniably successful no matter how much some of us prefer games that are much broader in what the rules enable and encourage.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to make VtM more accessible (and thus more likely to be adapted to other forms of entertainment), narrowing it's base/default scope is a completely valid approach to take. You still have to do it well, and then manage it well, but if done right there's no reason to expect it wouldn't work to make the brand easier to get back to the mainstream.<br /> <br /> From a non-interaction fiction writer's point of view the &quot;anything can find a home in here,&quot; kitchen sink is not best. How is a novel writer, or TV script doctor supposed to know how to make their story more VtM-esque if there is no core VtM loop people are 100% expecting. D&amp;D's narrower play-loop is much, much easier to write in if your goal is to keep some level of brand consistency. Without it you're way more likely to get style over substance, and lose the edge you need to get back to mainstream status.<br /> <br /> Even for interactive fiction it causes problems. There's whole sets of memes about how nobody actually finishes Elder Scrolls games. You have this gigantic sandbox, and the main questline is the easiest thing on Earth to completely forget about, and dozens of hours later, you feel like you've played enough of the game to last you for ages... and you never got past the mandatory intro main quest missions. If that kind of broadness was good for video-game writing, you'd wouldn't see that tendency to get so wrapped up in side-quests and exploration that you never play the main game that is so often lamented about super-sandboxy game design.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#ff3333\"><b>Please leave the Thread. This isn't the place to criticize other posters. If you have a problem, then report them.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T07:29:36-08:00","id":1504038,"title":"","content":"I've gotten a bit weary of the discourse, but I did just want to note the one thing here on the &quot;the narrowest game is the most accessible and most facilitates success&quot; concept. Part of D&amp;D 5e's success, certainly the successes that comes from having seemingly managed to facilitate a live play explosion overnight is that a ton of these especially popular APs are efforts to push 5e into all sorts of wild nonsensical directions the game even kinda sorta creaks at going into, but they nevertheless go into.<br /> <br /> Dimension 20 for instance is a consistent attempt at genre and mechanics mashups that have gone from everything from relatively standardish D&amp;D, to attempting to do Fantasy Regency Drama D&amp;D and the like. The online 5e branding ecosphere, as it were, are people pushing D&amp;D 5e in as many directions as they can try to, and Wizards totally wants their game to feel like it can be all things to all people, even if one would prefer that they not, and note their game is in fact super not great at that. <br /> <br /> You can certainly argue that the game breaks apart and doesn't really help people wanting to push it that way, but they are clearly wanting and trying to nevertheless, and Wizards is happy to let you think that you can. <br /> <br /> Now, it's certainly the case that in chasing Hollywood success, a thing VtM consistently fails in chasing, yet desperately continues to chase, narrow as possible is more helpful for your average screenwriter/production team needing to make an elevator pitch. But as a game? Outside of the supernova of success that is CoC in Japan, narrow gets you Pendragon, a beloved little borderline indie darling at this point that Chaosium nevertheless republishes to an audience of mostly regulars that has never, in my entire time of gaming, ever really managed to broadly penetrate outside of its hardcore devotees, and whose structure and rules definitely call for and mechanically enforce the narrowest playstyle possible. Achilli himself was effusive in his praise for Pendragon and at one point compared it to what he wants for VtM and why it being super narrow and forcing that from within the game is great, as far as everyone trying to parse the goals of his tenure and the direction they leave behind. Regardless all something to consider when weighing on an rpg audience level if one approach is truly better than another.<br /> <br /> Really though, the main thing helpful to VtM 5th as it currently stands regardless is not whether it is wide, or whether it is narrow, it is that it has a promotional budget that compared to any other instance of the game is a truly godlike thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T07:39:02-08:00","id":1504040,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure VTM is the perfect thing for Hollywood.<br /> -Game of thrones $$$<br /> -...But with &quot;superheroes&quot; $$$$<br /> -...and less expensive costumes $$<br /> -Real world political commentary $$$$ <br /> <br /> It's a surer recipe than four dwarves with laser pointers and a large nugget of gold. If you just avoid the metaplot... oh damn. It's all ruined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T08:01:23-08:00","id":1504043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504040#post1504040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure VTM is the perfect thing for Hollywood.<br /> -Game of thrones $$$<br /> -...But with &quot;superheroes&quot; $$$$<br /> -...and less expensive costumes $$<br /> -Real world political commentary $$$$<br /> <br /> It's a surer recipe than four dwarves with laser pointers and a large nugget of gold. If you just avoid the metaplot... oh damn. It's all ruined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires aren't really big anymore like they were during Twilight, or even during True Blood. Or even during Vampire Diaries! All of which the companies behind the WoD seemed like they very snootily refused to try and capitalize on even though the entire point of their very original success as White Wolf was that they tapped into a cultural zeitgeist flare and rode it out until that flare guttered out. (There was one borderline condescending, too late, barely there VtR almost mini supp about the whole Vampire Romance era).<br /> <br /> If the Interview with the Vampire remake becomes a huge smash, maybe... but probably not by this point (which is a shame, it's pretty good).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T09:22:59-08:00","id":1504052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504043#post1504043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires aren't really big anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>Make em big then. Things like zombies or heroes or vampires go up and down, but the driving force behind the ups is quality and the driving force behind the downs is a lack of it. I don't think of oversaturation as a direct determiner of decline (unless someone's insisting on an interdependent shared universe where I feel like I have to catch up on everything just to fully enjoy what's current *Marvel*) Oversaturation is really a product of lazy producers churning out crap that's dressed up as it. If every zombie film was great and the genre adapted beyond regurgitating it's basic principles it would have never died out. <br /> Yes, that's a bit of a stretch since zombies are kind of unreasonable in it's own setting (I can buy into Superman punching apart an asteroid to save the earth or even fooling a Pulitzer prize winning journalist with a alter ego that's often in proximity to her, but a bunch of slow people who are defeated by chain link fences overrunning a modern mechanized military? not at all.) But VTM actually does well because, y'know, it doesn't stop at &quot;vampires&quot; or focus on people surviving the vampires, it depicts vampires as complex people. Vampires will always have the potential to work because they're larger than life figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T09:34:15-08:00","id":1504053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504052#post1504052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Make em big then. Things like zombies or heroes or vampires go up and down, but the driving force behind the ups is quality and the driving force behind the downs is a lack of it. I don't think of oversaturation as a direct determiner of decline (unless someone's insisting on an interdependent shared universe where I feel like I have to catch up on everything just to fully enjoy what's current *Marvel*) Oversaturation is really a product of lazy producers churning out crap that's dressed up as it. If every zombie film was great and the genre adapted beyond regurgitating it's basic principles it would have never died out.<br /> Yes, that's a bit of a stretch since zombies are kind of unreasonable in it's own setting (I can buy into Superman punching apart an asteroid to save the earth or even fooling a Pulitzer prize winning journalist with a alter ego that's often in proximity to her, but a bunch of slow people who are defeated by chain link fences overrunning a modern mechanized military? not at all.) But VTM actually does well because, y'know, it doesn't stop at &quot;vampires&quot; or focus on people surviving the vampires, it depicts vampires as complex people. Vampires will always have the potential to work because they're larger than life figures.</div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot will Hollywood into caring about something that is not, at the moment, making enough of a pop cultural imprint in wider audiences or even popular subcultures for them to care about. It is telling that the even moderately major efforts at vampire media things in recent years have been basically comedic parodies, or an ultimately so far minor set of shows on AMC. <br /> <br /> The only hope you or anyone really have for VtM to go mainstream is for Hollywood's endless quest to regurgitate every even semi old IP resulting in a Twilight Revival both happening and being successful, and the people doing VtM being able to hold their nose this time and jump on the ride in some related way. But when even the much ballyhooed True Blood revival just got shot down before it could even get going (and that show was a big ol big deal when it was popular), odds even for that are low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T10:31:33-08:00","id":1504058,"title":"","content":"Vampires will always be a popular type of monster and lets not write them off yet. All it takes is just one good movie or horror writer with his or her own spin on the lore to make it good and get people interested again. As long as the characters are interesting and flawed and there is a good story and we don't have Gary &amp; Mary Sue cardboard characters then I'm sure interest will be peaked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-28-2023, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T14:33:07-08:00","id":1504073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504058#post1504058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires will always be a popular type of monster and lets not write them off yet. All it takes is just one good movie or horror writer with his or her own spin on the lore to make it good and get people interested again. As long as the characters are interesting and flawed and there is a good story and we don't have Gary &amp; Mary Sue cardboard characters then I'm sure interest will be peaked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be real with you here, the last two really, truly big popular culture vampire runs of living memory post the 80s-90s Goth cultural movement riding high being Twilight and True Blood means that interest in vampires had, ehhmm, very little of the things you are hoping for (I kid True Blood. I kid because Iove, sort of, if I squint while looking from an angle. But mostly just at Russel Edgington).<br /> <br /> Popular= good are not the same things sometimes, and even often. It less takes a story being good and more, like many pop culture trends, just somehow tapping in *juuust right* to a popular appeal or sentiment at somehow at just the right time so successfully, that every other clever media critic person rushes to write a thinkpiece about how we should have seen that coming the whole time in hindsight.<br /> <br /> Might vampires come out of nowhere and do that again? Maybe! But nothing from the current successes of such things suggests it.<br /> <br /> We're otherwise mostly just getting the usual &quot;it's been coming up on over ten years since the thing we laughed at for being dumb happened, it's time to be contrarian and say it was totally cool actually&quot;, which isn't enough to sustain a full pop culture revival on its own. (Or again, the True Blood revival would not have just been killed off).<br /> <br /> I mean Vampire Diaries ended in 2017 I suppose, but it was nowhere near the cultural explosion of the other two by the end of its run (or even the beginning, where granted it was regardless still crazy popular), and also, brace yourself for being an old, that was basically six years ago (the other two, obviously, even older).<br /> <br /> VtM the tabletop roleplaying game itself, as far as its 5th edition is 5 years old now. If anyone in the company really does have some goal of recapturing the wider cultural zeitgeist or even simply of Vampire's previous level of prominence/success in gaming, while I'm sure the game has done well enough just fine to justify continuing to publish it, it has definitely not done that first or second thing. And whatever all you can and could say about that potentially reflecting the game itself, it also reflects pretty well how cultural trends move on and leave things behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 02-28-2023, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T19:37:14-08:00","id":1504098,"title":"","content":"There's a Blade Remake coming out, remember. Blade may not revive vampires by himself, but he (hopefully) won't hurt, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T16:44:13-08:00","id":1504144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504073#post1504073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to be real with you here, the last two really, truly big popular culture vampire runs of living memory post the 80s-90s Goth cultural movement riding high being Twilight and True Blood means that interest in vampires had, ehhmm, very little of the things you are hoping for (I kid True Blood. I kid because Iove, sort of, if I squint while looking from an angle. But mostly just at Russel Edgington).<br /> <br /> We're otherwise mostly just getting the usual &quot;it's been coming up on over ten years since the thing we laughed at for being dumb happened, it's time to be contrarian and say it was totally cool actually&quot;, which isn't enough to sustain a full pop culture revival on its own. (Or again, the True Blood revival would not have just been killed off).<br /> <br /> I mean Vampire Diaries ended in 2017 I suppose, but it was nowhere near the cultural explosion of the other two by the end of its run (or even the beginning, where granted it was regardless still crazy popular), and also, brace yourself for being an old, that was basically six years ago (the other two, obviously, even older).</div> </div> </div> </div>A very good vampire fiction movie is <i>The Hunger</i> (also called <i>The Riddle of Immortality</i>). Really puts across how vampires in various stories are otherworldy, beautiful, wise, and exceptional. One of my favourite movies, the mood, pacing, scenery and atmosphere are very nice and interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T20:42:06-08:00","id":1504172,"title":"","content":"You dont want mainstream, you want successful and good with a large enough following to sustain it. Vampire in the 90s was peak, and I damn near missed it, coming in at the time of Gehenna, so I am is as young as they can be when Vampire was popular and could have played it and not be horriblely inappropriate and I'm closer to 40 than hip 20 year old (jesus that hurts). See Paradox wanted to take WoD mainstream and for that they took a cleaver to the setting and lore to make it accessible but released these in universe prentensious faction source books and I am an older fan and was still lost. The problem is that VtM was a dark cynical setting written in the early 90s by people who lived in the Reagan Era who happend to be very punk and goth. You know very church friendly people. My kind of people (the Vampire people not the chirch people). The problem was, Vampire at its best is problematic, and it needs to be. It was crass, dark, and obscene, each book offended some one on something. It was violent, dark, blood soaked sex and beautiful. It espoused the crimes of systemic oppression and made you part of it, why because you are playing a game of personal horror where you are a blood drinking parasitic corpse. If you didn't get message that this game was filled with pitch black satire that was heavy handed with its messaging then keep playing cause the jokes on you, buy more product so we can keep the lights on and telling you that this world is horrible and so are you. Then we got some suits and activists come in who didn't get the joke, didn't understand the nessisary ugliness. That this is a Game set in the World of Darkness, where you are the monsters, who sometimes fights monsters but monsters you shall be and you can't be more on the chin than that. I guess we are just going to keep getting some variation of the trench coat katanas (not that there is anything wrong with that perse)(trying to make this a game of cool Vampire heroes)<br /> This was a game made by outcasts for outcasts and thats okay, and we already sacrificed so much to try to make it mainstream and it is hurting the very brand it's trying save.<br /> Best we can do, salvage what we can, nuture the next generation of players, keep the old lore alive, and can some one please write a God damn Vampire story that's good, and not a love story, and if you know of one let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T21:27:35-08:00","id":1504176,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, I'm not overall saying whether mainstream is good or bad, I'm just noting, odds of it ever being such again are super low, and if that has been an actual goal of the current VtM making team, they have definitely not met it in any real sense. And to a certain extent, that might be impossible for them to do anyway, as things stand culturally.<br /> <br /> (Well, no, the one nice thing about mainstream and gaming is that it's certainly easier to find players and games and even be spoiled for choice when something is popular, there is that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T22:02:21-08:00","id":1504177,"title":"","content":"I suppose the one other thing I would otherwise note is, ultimately, while not as once it was, this game is five years old. It hasn't folded. While not one that has pushed it into some gaming upper stratosphere, it has its own fanbase who have probably never known anything but this version of VtM at this point, and part of the entire goal was to get said new fanbase. And if they get kudos along the way from the older fans who feel vindicated by this edition's choices (for all that I happen to personally feel those choices are ill made, smug, and vengeful), hey, bonus.<br /> <br /> That doesn't make the game good, it just means that, as far as this theme of &quot;ignoring their customer base&quot; and all that sort of thing I'm seeing, they aren't. They've just decided what they want their customer base to be, what that marketing budget thereby goes to, and who they have decided is irrelevant to it. And since, again, we're talking about a five year old gameline, that means 5th edition has another year to go to have lasted roughly/almost as long as either Second Edition or Revised. As a product that exists in the world of ttrpg gaming, I don't like it, but it's sustaining itself seemingly just fine.<br /> <br /> Also it's a bit.. I don't know, you have the repeated horrible choices made in various 5th ed books/content/marketing/etc. at this point as far as any basic sensitivity to the experiences of various ethnicities and marginalized populations, and yet at the exact same time people who gripe about 5th ed griping that it's &quot;activism run amok&quot;. Someone more clever than I would probably want to jump on that to claim &quot;clearly that means they're taking some mythical correct middle ground, where it's just offensive enough, as a treat!&quot;, but I don't know, to me that feels more than a bit grim in a &quot;well I don't feel like I have a place in the current edition, and maybe I never really did in all the previous ones either&quot; kind of way.<br /> <br /> There's something wild about watching some of the writers and devs and current fans otherwise pick out the most reactionary takes they can find of V5 criticism as far as &quot;this is the only real reason anyone ever dislikes this game&quot; to dismiss any other critique of it in terms of craft or playability, and basically lean on that to act like their own Second Inquisition Brazil content shaped missteps are clearly not even worthy of note, even though they somehow keep finding ways to happen. And yet at the same time that happens, there is still this full throated gripe that keeps popping up about VtM no longer being free to be offensive or what have you.<br /> <br /> Maybe what I'm saying then is that perhaps the game doesn't really deserve to have mainstream popularity again, even if it could. Maybe it shouldn't.<br /> <br /> I suppose that was just stream of consciousnessing my weariness of the state of the discourse these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 03-02-2023, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T02:04:50-08:00","id":1504185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504176#post1504176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh hey, I'm not overall saying whether mainstream is good or bad</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so subjective and full of variables that it could as well change based on what day of the week (or month) it is currently.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T02:19:28-08:00","id":1504186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504185#post1504185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is so subjective and full of variables that it could as well change based on what day of the week (or month) it is currently.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really not sure what you're trying to say in reply to me there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T02:30:18-08:00","id":1504189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504186#post1504186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm really not sure what you're trying to say in reply to me there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was me putting forth an idea in regard to what can happen when a work of art, fiction, or culture moves in it's popularity and reach towards what is called conventional or mainstream. I consider it that when this occurs, then it can very well be hard to evaluate how various issues and events related to this particular piece of culture are changed or affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T02:56:27-08:00","id":1504193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504189#post1504189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was me putting forth an idea in regard to what can happen when a work of art, fiction, or culture moves in it's popularity and reach towards what is called conventional or mainstream. I consider it that when this occurs, then it can very well be hard to evaluate how various issues and events related to this particular piece of culture are changed or affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit.. non sequitur-y to reply like that then? It's just a note that something achieving broad scale cultural notability is not always the same thing as whether it's good or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T11:23:02-08:00","id":1504277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501283-do-you-think-vtm-will-ever-become-mainstream?p=1504098#post1504098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Blade Remake coming out, remember. Blade may not revive vampires by himself, but he (hopefully) won't hurt, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard that movie was in limbo for the time being and I'm not sure how scary a PG-13 rated movie will be when it comes to a character like Blade and how do you top Wesley Snipes performance as Blade. I can't think of to many current actors who could pull it off currently. This generation gap thing sucks as I can't even name a top shelf action hero or heroine under the age 40-45 anymore like I used to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T11:27:06-08:00","id":1504278,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> I'm still hopeful in the film industry despite my recent posts on how I feel about Hollywood current skill of storytelling and think there will be a crop of films that will make people want to go out to see them. Hence my original statement interest in vampires will be there and it's just waiting for the right writer, cast of actors, director and etc to come together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T19:01:41-08:00","id":1504312,"title":"","content":"If the intention is the VTM series, this has material for adaptations like in games, movies, books, novels and several other things, so this is not impossible, it all depends on someone being able to make a highly successful adaptation. Now, one thing that scares me is that if this happens it could draw unwanted attention and VTM as well as other WOD branches need to change to avoid problems. That said, in part, I prefer the VTM to remain something more underground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T13:05:11-08:00","id":1504969,"title":"","content":"I do believe VTM may recover it's position as the 2nd best known TTRPG, but they must put their shit together. Nowadays there are 3 lines going on under Vampire, VTM 1-20 Ed, VTR, and VTM 5 Ed. Maybe a V6 going full Requiem or coming back towards Masquerade may recover the franchise and pacify the fan base. I imagine if there are other medias related it can bring more people back, as Stranger Things made with D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}